  "GL_C_RC5 task147": "Kill a pmc with the SIG Sauer Vertical Foregrip KeyMod (Black)",
  "GL_C_RC5 successMT": "I can't believe you actually did this. Are you insane? What the heck. You must really, really care about recoil control. Well, good job. ...you want something for it? What, I'm an angel. Uhm... here, there's a little something in the corner of your shelter you never noticed. Go grab that.",
  "GL_C_RC5 acceptMT": "This... is hell...",

  "675e7bb9a29a9242665cb6de name": "Big iron",
  "675e7bb9a29a9242665cb6de description": "Revolvers are an interesting weapon for sure. They're the size of a pistol, but most pack the punch of a sniper rifle. The cost is, well, literal monetary cost, as well as recoil and ammo capacity. Every shot counts here!",
  "675e7c015ee255313925c564": "Kill 10 enemies with a revolver",
  "6833712380620b7e8eb1ac66": "Inflict 800 damage with a revolver",
  "675e7bb9a29a9242665cb6de successMT": "Nice aim! Make sure you're hitting important places, not much worth in shooting the arms here or legs here.",
  "675e7bb9a29a9242665cb6de acceptMT": "on his hip",

  "675e7c28ab10a437be2f8c7b name": "Between the eyes (and the lungs)",
  "675e7c28ab10a437be2f8c7b description": "Due to low ammo capacity, you really have to hit important stuff with revolvers. You should only be aiming for the head and thorax, you don't have enough ammo to kill quickly through the flesh, even with specialized ammo.",
  "675e7d18c08a62a84029114b": "Land 15 headshots with revolvers",
  "675e7d2653fa765860752ea0": "Land 30 thorax shots with revolvers",
  "675e7c28ab10a437be2f8c7b successMT": "Yep, that's about it. See ya.",
  "675e7c28ab10a437be2f8c7b acceptMT": "Happy to take him out, actually",

  "675e7c632c112b09b8ca85b8 name": "Aiming? What for?",
  "675e7c632c112b09b8ca85b8 description": "You know those old western movies where they just take the revolver right out of the holster and fire without hardly aiming. Yeah, it's kinda cool, kinda silly. But 'point firing' is actually a very useful thing. Revolvers seem like a good thing to practice with! ...Hey, speaking of cowboy movies...",
  "683371d9994b5c3ec5a270e6": "Kill 30 enemies with revolvers while point / hip firing",
  "675e7d991baa549533f01457": "Kill 10 enemies with revolvers while wearing the Kinda Cowboy hat",
  "675e7c632c112b09b8ca85b8 successMT": "It's highhhhh noon. Actually, it's probably midnight. You're playing Tarkov, admit it.",
  "675e7c632c112b09b8ca85b8 acceptMT": "Hurray, a somewhat fun quest!",

  "675e7d3553464ec26df97607 name": "Reserved for him",
  "675e7d3553464ec26df97607 description": "You know the military reserve base, correct? There's this squad of guys that acts like they own the place, it's kind of annoying. Put a round through him, make sure he remembers it when he respawns.",
  "675e7c49a5a7bac8f9c84aab": "Kill Gluhar with the Rsh-12",
  "675e7d3553464ec26df97607 successMT": "Well done! He'll be keeping an eye out for you from now on, that's for sure.",
  "675e7d3553464ec26df97607 acceptMT": "Happy to take him out, actually",

  "675e7db469cbd38e5f4c0c16 name": "Master of firearms: Revolvers",
  "675e7db469cbd38e5f4c0c16 description": "This likely isn't your first T5 weapon challenge, so I'll spare you the details. I'm gonna let you off easy on the 200ds here, but to make up for it, I expect very high kill counts for the RSh-12, got it?",
  "675e7dca28b829a57b4eba6e": "Kill 5 PMCs with the CR 200DS",
  "675e7dddf1843ed9d668c576": "Kill 10 PMCs with the CR 50DS",
  "675e7deaf1c44de99195b448": "Kill 30 PMCs with the RSh-12",
  "68337397e77e7ff33b47b8c4": "Kill 60 enemies with revolvers while point / hip firing",
  "683373981bb1574b70d6c4fb": "Kill 30 enemies with revolvers while wearing the Kinda Cowboy hat",
  "675e7db469cbd38e5f4c0c16 successMT": "Master of the sidearms! Great job.",
  "675e7db469cbd38e5f4c0c16 acceptMT": "This makes the third quest in Tarkov that requires cowboy hats. Interesting.",

  "675f10ec444183edfe380e00 name": "Pump it up",
  "675f10ec444183edfe380e00 description": "Despite how big Tarkov is, there's still plenty of buildings and other small areas. If you want to dominate CQC, shotguns are the way to go. Slugs, buckshots, flechettes, plenty of ammo choices, all extremely deadly. Don't forget that you're locked in single fire!",
  "675f1100da2d5f7c8256f68a": "Kill 15 enemies with shotguns",
  "6833c4da76050692568b2120": "Inflict 1500 damage to enemies with shotguns",
  "675f10ec444183edfe380e00 successMT": "Do you prefer pump actions or semi-autos? Pump action is more satisfying, but semi-auto is more effective.",
  "675f10ec444183edfe380e00 acceptMT": "One of the more satisfying weapon catagories",

  "675f1123a9ae958e9716e16e name": "Shoot 'em everywhere (but the arms)",
  "675f1123a9ae958e9716e16e description": "Shotguns are great because just about everywhere you can shoot will be effective one way or another. Legs will chew through quickly, but plenty of ammo will also get through any armor just by breaking it down. The only real 'bad' place to shoot is the arms, it just doens't do enough damage. Practice shooting everywhere but the arms (you'll probably hit the arms anyways, going for thorax)",
  "675f118c5a997eaef5bd92e7": "Land 15 headshots with shotguns",
  "675f119efe49c83b17eea1e7": "Land 150 thorax or stomach shots with shotguns (each pellet counts!)",
  "675f11ac79f75c0698367f65": "Land 300 leg shots with shotguns (each pellet counts!)",
  "675f1123a9ae958e9716e16e successMT": "Shotguns are deadly, aren't they? They're vicious, even at medium ranges. Keep aiming in that middle third, and you'll be all good.",
  "675f1123a9ae958e9716e16e acceptMT": "Gonna shred some folks",

  "675f116b93022a000de71964 name": "The grinder",
  "675f116b93022a000de71964 description": "Shotguns are great because just about everywhere you can shoot will be effective one way or another. Legs will chew through quickly, but plenty of ammo will also get through any armor just by breaking it down. The only real 'bad' place to shoot is the arms, it just doens't do enough damage. Practice shooting everywhere but the arms (you'll probably hit the arms anyways, going for thorax)",
  "683376b8e4c55f5894130553": "Deal 1000 damage to enemy armour with shotguns",
  "675f116b93022a000de71964 successMT": "Nicely done! Most slugs aren't too effective against armour, but some buckshot and especially the flechette rounds just disentegrate it.",
  "675f116b93022a000de71964 acceptMT": "Those poor plates.",

  "675f11c1f4909a5a85d61000 name": "Bringing the facility back online",
  "675f11c1f4909a5a85d61000 description": "That factory is quite the death trap, isn't it? Nowhere to hide, all close quarters, and the boss there is an absolute menace with his Saiga-12.    ...hmm... what if you became the boss of factory?",
  "675f11395703e3a9f9b2b2c8": "Kill Tagilla with the Saiga-12",
  "675f11c1f4909a5a85d61000 successMT": "You da real boss now! Good stuff, man. Own that factory",
  "675f11c1f4909a5a85d61000 acceptMT": "That's a lot of health to chew through with a shotgun...",

  "675f1210b9608eaeb3b06cf2 name": "Master of firearms: Shotguns",
  "675f1210b9608eaeb3b06cf2 description": "Alright, you know what to do. Every shotgun. Paint the world red. Let's get 15 with each, alright? Hmm... You can combine the 153 and 155, I don't mind. And just get 5 on the toz. Shred some armour for me in the meantime! Watching numbers go up is fun, for some reason.",
  "675f1234e68b7fddbee8b0d9": "Kill 15 pmcs with the KS-23M",
  "675f1241bab1970848669abf": "Kill 15 pmcs with the M3 Super 90",
  "675f124c97cd0eb02fc61b7b": "Kill 15 pmcs with the M590A1",
  "675f12572cfef656e6f9bbb2": "Kill 15 pmcs with the M870",
  "675f12638861179deaaeefd3": "Kill 15 pmcs with the MP-133",
  "675f126ef1f2afbebf9594c8": "Kill 15 pmcs with the MP-153 / 155",
  "675f12909830926dd42f6c97": "Kill 15 pmcs with the MP-43-1C (or Sawed Off)",
  "675f129ca346a73c896ec661": "Kill 15 pmcs with the MTs-255-12",
  "675f12a874f0edd9e1bf9530": "Kill 15 pmcs with the Saiga-12 (semi or auto)",
  "67d7a7840acfd0746eedc34d": "Kill 15 pmcs with either AA-12",
  "675f12b3e24859ad3d917f1d": "Kill 5 pmcs with the TOZ-106",
  "683376d5192aaab39065c7b2": "Deal 4000 damage to enemy armour with shotguns",
  "675f1210b9608eaeb3b06cf2 successMT": "Truly an artist, you are! You are the master of shotguns",
  "675f1210b9608eaeb3b06cf2 acceptMT": "155 with the 155... oh, I have to use all of them? Oh well.",

  "675f1d11d6272e7d3db6ecdb name": "Sub machine guns aren't sub-par",
  "675f1d11d6272e7d3db6ecdb description": "Submachine guns are an excellect choice for Tarkov. They are perfect for close quarters, yet can perform decently at medium range. They aren't great for armor penetration, but their high fire rate makes up for it. Depending on the SMG, the recoil can range from rough to non-existent. Good luck!",
  "675f1d41b944910281386e23": "Kill 15 enemies with submachine guns",
  "68340f6d27a8db0b09539c08": "Inflict 1500 damage to enemies with submachine guns",
  "675f1d11d6272e7d3db6ecdb successMT": "How's it feel? Small, hopefully controllable, easy to handle, it's a great to shoot. It's a shame it doesn't do as much damage, though.",
  "675f1d11d6272e7d3db6ecdb acceptMT": "Sarah Michelle Gellar? Oh, Sub Machine Gun, ok.",

  "675f1d7dcd48c98ba19d329d name": "Sweep the legs, or drill the chest",
  "675f1d7dcd48c98ba19d329d description": "Sub machine guns, with maaybe the exception of the P90, are pretty weak against any high level armour. That means leg shots are going to be the main source of killing when it comes to these things. However, not everyone has good armour, and even those with good armour still have holes in that protection, so thorax shots are perfectly fine as well. And of course, a few headshots never hurt. Get on it.",
  "675f1e6cc2af2044cb1c703e": "Land 10 headshots with SMGs",
  "675f1e7db056f7a66c87d99f": "Land 80 thorax shots with SMGs",
  "675f1e9269e97cc2c5805bfe": "Land 150 leg shots with SMGs",
  "675f1d7dcd48c98ba19d329d successMT": "Good recoil control. Legs are pretty easy to munch through with the right stuff, eh?",
  "675f1d7dcd48c98ba19d329d acceptMT": "Fast fire rate, fast completion",

  "675f1e3e7df12a561797e9d0 name": "I said sweep those legs!",
  "675f1e3e7df12a561797e9d0 description": "So, truly... if you're using an SMG, you're most likely going for the legs. Yes, there are a few exceptions that can deal with mid-level armour, but you're going for the squishy bits most of the time. You know a place that can't be armoured (for some reason)? Yep, same as last time. Knock 'em over!",
  "68341164bb749f3bd48a3957": "Destroy ('black') 40 enemy legs with SMGs",
  "675f1e3e7df12a561797e9d0 successMT": "Good recoil control. Legs are pretty easy to munch through with the right stuff, eh?",
  "675f1e3e7df12a561797e9d0 acceptMT": "Fast fire rate, fast completion",

  "675f1eeef00aecbfe2ce2864 name": "Machine to the medic",
  "675f1eeef00aecbfe2ce2864 description": "That Sanitar guy... man. You have not seen what he has done, let me tell you. Normally, these boss hunting missions are just a fun challenge, but this... I need you to put this guy down. I know he'll revive, he always does, but put him down anyways. His... 'work' on God's creations are unholy. Kill him with his own gun, I want him to remember this.",
  "675f1dc66ecdf14174049903": "Kill Sanitar with SPECIFICALLY the Kedr-B (others will not count!)",
  "675f1eeef00aecbfe2ce2864 successMT": "Thank you. I know he'll be back, but, I'm glad we could at least do that.",
  "675f1eeef00aecbfe2ce2864 acceptMT": "I don't think I want to know.",

  "675f20613c445e740cccc65a name": "Master of firearms: SMGs",
  "675f20613c445e740cccc65a description": "Haven't had enough yet? Alright, let's see you use a lot of those SMGs on the real guys then! I won't be too picky on similar smgs, but I want you to obliterate every leg that isn't your own.",
  "675f2077a36868feedec3a65": "Kill 10 PMCs with any MP5",
  "675f21431d9fef06520ed343": "Kill 10 PMCs with the MP7 (A1 OR A2)",
  "675f2176d6cbd1951fe7132e": "Kill 10 PMCs with either MP9",
  "675f21a903e2257150de43b0": "Kill 10 PMCs with the MPX",
  "675f21b66fad7ae4e2a64bf6": "Kill 10 PMCs with the P90",
  "675f21e661c0e85dd6005c2c": "Kill 10 PMCs with the PP-19-01",
  "675f21f6aeaf154aef2d01c0": "Kill 10 PMCs with the PP-9 Klin",
  "675f221f5966269208fbb0c4": "Kill 10 PMCs with the PP-91 Kedr OR Kedr-B (91-01)",
  "675f22335ad16666896fd863": "Kill 10 PMCs with the PPSh-41",
  "675f22474ff344147ce9336d": "Kill 10 PMCs with the Saiga-9",
  "675f226117042005a2fdeb56": "Kill 10 PMCs with the SR-2M",
  "675f226fe69d0a1ec8f7fe1a": "Kill 10 PMCs with the STM-9",
  "675f228d6ec07df722fbfff9": "Kill 10 PMCs with the UMP-45",
  "675f229f21f7510635be9f99": "Kill 10 PMCs with the Vector .45",
  "675f22b518a0ac496e5fd771": "Kill 10 PMCs with the Vector 9x19",
  "675f1531c304f0dbfa6d7cf8": "Kill 10 PMCs with the IMI UZI (NOT PRO)",
  "675f153d855f25283352fc71": "Kill 10 PMCs with either of the IMI UZI PRO's",
  "68340e438b47c4a536003328": "Destroy ('black)' 200 enemy legs with SMGs",
  "675f20613c445e740cccc65a successMT": "Master of the SMGs! That was quite a lot of PMC kills, well done. Take a break.",
  "675f20613c445e740cccc65a acceptMT": "9x19=190, no prob- Oh wait, nevermind.",

  "675f239281e627eeb22cf704 name": "Click-Clack",
  "675f239281e627eeb22cf704 description": "Bolt action Sniper rifles are the most deadly single-shot weapons in existance when it comes to small-arms. Their downside, obviously, is a heavy, very slow-firing, low-capacity weapon, where one shot makes or breaks it. Let's do a fun challenge this time: You have to hit headshots for this task. Aim high!",
  "675f2425fbb32c77a3f30f86": "Kill 8 enemies with headshots with sniper rifles",
  "675f239281e627eeb22cf704 successMT": "How are bolt-actions feeling for ya? It's pretty hit or miss with people... no pun intended.",
  "675f239281e627eeb22cf704 acceptMT": "Slow and steady",

  "675f248a8f23738f582f4cf4 name": "One or two?",
  "675f248a8f23738f582f4cf4 description": "One to the head, two to the thorax. Which will it be? Headshots are more important... but thorax will hurt them badly.",
  "675f257f88bc009ff5af1ac8": "Land 20 headshots with sniper rifles",
  "675f2595a1f5c9635998d0da": "Land 15 thorax shots with sniper rifles",
  "675f248a8f23738f582f4cf4 successMT": "Clean shots, man! Good job.",
  "675f25338f6c770ec54ddf62 acceptMT": "I prefer one, but sometimes two is all you can do.",

  "675f25338f6c770ec54ddf62 name": "The distance between us",
  "675f25338f6c770ec54ddf62 description": "Sniper rifles are entirely built for extreme distances. While it's still a large bullet that will hurt like heck at close range, they are meant to be accurate and deadly at ranges that no other weapon can compete in. I'll calculate some shots for you, let's build up a distance. (Explanation of this task: The distance between you and the enemy you shoot will be added to the counter. The further you are from your enemy, the faster you will complete this challenge!)",
  "68341a14799815f5d9179694": "Accumulate 4000 total shot distance with sniper rifles (see description)",
  "675f25338f6c770ec54ddf62 successMT": "Clean shots, man! Good job.",
  "675f248a8f23738f582f4cf4 acceptMT": "They are long range, to be fair.",

  "675f25c70e47562aeab94138 name": "Hawk-eye",
  "675f25c70e47562aeab94138 description": "You're run into the Goons already, correct? That one guy, who makes no noise when he runs... he confuses me. You're a better sniper than him, show him that no audio won't save him.",
  "675f24a74a05264a82602a94": "Snipe Birdeye with an M700 or Sako TRG",
  "675f25c70e47562aeab94138 successMT": "Very well done! That's not easy to do. Another death for that goon",
  "675f25c70e47562aeab94138 acceptMT": "What a cheater...",

  "675f26cdece5e7b5f0ed152c name": "Master of firearms: Sniper rifles",
  "675f26cdece5e7b5f0ed152c description": "Alright, sniper. Here's your final challenge: 10 PMC kills with every sniper you can find in Tarkov. Headshots aren't required, but I recommend them. Also, I want to see how much distance you can gather doing this... steady your aim, friend.",
  "675f27811c87ad2d5f2feabf": "Kill 10 PMCs with the AXMC or Sako TRG",
  "675f279a20a401fa1e312d99": "Kill 10 PMCs with the DVL-10",
  "675f27abe2368f7f4db74e36": "Kill 10 PMCs with the M700",
  "675f27efb6fded7b54aadab4": "Kill 10 PMCs with the Mosin (Infantry OR Sniper varient)",
  "675f287c05d2a033c215e90e": "Kill 10 PMCs with the MP-18",
  "675f28916ee2ce3c6ea5a072": "Kill 10 PMCs with the SV-98",
  "675f28a5d09f8e40b3d689fa": "Kill 10 PMCs with the T-5000",
  "675f28b434bb6dbdba9a89c8": "Kill 10 PMCs with the VPO-215",
  "68341aa44d195ad2b7abba9c": "Accumulate 40000 total shot distance with sniper rifles",
  "675f26cdece5e7b5f0ed152c successMT": "Very well done! You are now the master of the sniper rifles. Go on, marksman!",
  "675f26cdece5e7b5f0ed152c acceptMT": "80 kills... I only need 80 shots. Eh, maybe 85.",

  "675f2afd766594bef110bece name": "Hot potatoes",
  "675f2afd766594bef110bece description": "Grenades can be a complete game changes, if you use them correctly. Lethal grenades, unsuprisingly, are great for blowing up your enemies. Let's try that, shall we?",
  "675f2b27f50938bd2efa2db4": "Kill 3 enemies with grenades",
  "675f2afd766594bef110bece successMT": "Nice throw! Let's keep working on that.",
  "675f2afd766594bef110bece acceptMT": "Hit 'em with the layup",

  "675f2bb9d1eccf8833c0d8c6 name": "No escape",
  "675f2bb9d1eccf8833c0d8c6 description": "You know what's even better than a grenade? An impact grenade. They detonate the moment they land, meaning that there's absolutely nothing your enemy can do to escape it, assuming you throw it correctly. Go give it a try.",
  "675f2ba80b383aa080ba0fe1": "Kill 5 enemies with impact grenades",
  "675f2bb9d1eccf8833c0d8c6 successMT": "Good throwing, man! Now let's swap to tacticals",
  "675f2bb9d1eccf8833c0d8c6 acceptMT": "Quite a rude way to kill someone, tbh",

  "675f2c075bbac044aa287c5f name": "Dazed and Destroyed",
  "675f2c075bbac044aa287c5f description": "Tactical grenades might not be able to kill an enemy outright, but it can leave them as good as dead. A good flash grenade on an enemy completely ruins them. Kill 5 enemies that can't see you.",
  "675f2c2f42f30bc068216579": "Kill 5 stunned enemies",
  "675f2c075bbac044aa287c5f successMT": "On the bright side (heh), you probably took them out with a headshot, so they didn't feel much pain. I hope you took them out with a headshot, anyways...",
  "675f2c075bbac044aa287c5f acceptMT": "Nevermind, that's more rude.",

  "675f2d630fb5e018bc7f35c3 name": "Fusing together",
  "675f2d630fb5e018bc7f35c3 description": "Lethal grenades have various fuses. Some are shorter, some are longer. Short fuses are great for suprising an enemy with a quick grenade, leaving little room for them to leave. Longer fuses are great for throwing further and bouncing around things. The M67 in partiuclar is great for baiting, as the long fuse time makes it more difficult to kill outright but will still force the enemy out. Try out the different fuse times and see what works best for you.",
  "675f2db3afedb9672ce943de": "Kill 3 enemies with grenades that have a fuse shorter than 3 seconds",
  "675f2dd9106c5bc59e2dabc2": "Kill 3 enemies with grenades that have a fuse longer than 3 seconds",
  "675f2df4c7a8d6e8d43b4e62": "Kill an enemy with the M67",
  "675f2d630fb5e018bc7f35c3 successMT": "Did you end up preferring the shorter or longer fuses? Both have their strengths and weaknesses, and are highly contextual.",
  "675f2d630fb5e018bc7f35c3 acceptMT": "Time for a little testing. With explosives.",

  "675f2e4f391bf57a07ef72aa name": "Hell's kitchen",
  "675f2e4f391bf57a07ef72aa description": "You know what time it is! Time to kill PMC with every thing in it's catagory! But you can't really kill people with flash grenades... hmm, oh well. Just kill some stunned PMCs.",
  "675f2ea0427cdf985426025d": "Kill 3 PMCs with the F-1",
  "675f2eea91bf5cf60db2f82d": "Kill 3 PMCs with the M67",
  "675f2f04dff8fb560f5f2736": "Kill 3 PMCs with the RDG-5",
  "675f2f146c463acddde73abd": "Kill 3 PMCs with the RGN",
  "675f2f24bfe5844b6c1bcade": "Kill 3 PMCs with the RGO",
  "675f2f3e61fe07d8944573a0": "Kill 3 PMCs with the VOG-17",
  "675f2f520d4db7112f864ba0": "Kill 3 PMCs with the VOG-25",
  "67d7abf221faa2d56a5b292d": "Kill 3 PMCs with the V40 Mini",
  "675f2f6c157eabdb12dc1dc4": "Kill 7 stunned PMCs",
  "675f2e4f391bf57a07ef72aa successMT": "Gordon Ramsey is pleased... ahem. You're clearly quite good with grenades. Keep using them effectively now that your training is done!",
  "675f2e4f391bf57a07ef72aa acceptMT": "Something about lamb sauce...",

  "675f65eb9f7bc9f7edd08f44 name": "Your gun has an issue",
  "675f65eb9f7bc9f7edd08f44 description": "Troubleshooting is a lifesaving skill when you're in trouble. The quicker you can identify what's wrong and fix it, the higher chance you can survive a malfunction. You can just run guns that are max durability... but that can get expensive. Besides, if you ever have to pick up a gun, that's likely not going to be at full durability. This is also why it's important to play smart no matter what, as you never know when something can go wrong. Though, if something is to go wrong, you need to know what to do about it. Prove to me you can clear a malfunction.",
  "675f660242d63294c7db2323": "Clear any malfunction once",
  "675f65eb9f7bc9f7edd08f44 successMT": "Did that malfunction happen before or after you got the kill? See, it can happen any time, and it's extremely problematic. Working on this skill is a very good idea.",
  "675f65eb9f7bc9f7edd08f44 acceptMT": "I think there are going to be some casualties in the weapons department by the end of this.",

  "675f667df71e49587d94fcc3 name": "Understanding the common cause",
  "675f667df71e49587d94fcc3 description": "Now that you've experienced a malfunction, let's talk about how it actually happens. There's a few different sources, but the worst offender is supressors. Some play nice with a gun, others really increase the wear and tear of a firearm. Go use the latter ones, and see what I mean.",
  "68316efdc4511ccadf70130f": "Kill 20 enemies while using a suppressor with >+70 durability burn",
  "675f667df71e49587d94fcc3 successMT": "See? Even after just a couple hours, your firearm needs some repairing now. ",
  "675f667df71e49587d94fcc3 acceptMT": "My poor firearms",

  "675f66c0fd6af76747f35f9e name": "Should've gotten the extended warrenty",
  "675f66c0fd6af76747f35f9e description": "You can clear a malfunction from your favorite gun, sure. What about others? You can't use the same firearm the whole time, at least, with those traders forcing you to do a bunch of different stuff. Can you clear jams from other weapon types?",
  "68316efb0056ef4520de3f0d": "Clear a malfunction from an Assault Rifle (or Carbine)",
  "68316e78af8fd73ab6c8a6e0": "Clear a malfunction from a Designated Marksman Rifle",
  "68316e794293800dcf0af408": "Clear a malfunction from a Light Machine Gun (only RPK-16 can jam!)",
  "68316e7a63833d3becd0ae23": "Clear a malfunction from a Pistol",
  "68316e7ae4d32f58c051debc": "Clear a malfunction from a Shotgun",
  "68316e7b2433d2cd6b1e0a7c": "Clear a malfunction from a Sub Machine Gun",
  "6835226fcd1b6b086d06b6f6": "Clear a malfunction from a Sniper rifle",
  "675f66c0fd6af76747f35f9e successMT": "How about that, you can! Good, you should be surviving just fine now.",
  "675f66c0fd6af76747f35f9e acceptMT": "This seems tedious",

  "675f67cb9d050e9f3e3de0f9 name": "That poor AKM",
  "675f67cb9d050e9f3e3de0f9 description": "Dust covers, suppressors, magazines... there's plenty of things that affect the durability burn and chance of malfunction. What if we combined all three of them at once? I want to show you how much these can affect the performance of a rifle..",
  "675f67e40cea1ee8d261c5a9": "Kill 10 enemies in one raid using an AKM that has no dust cover, a suppressor with >+70 durability burn, and a magazine with high or very high malfunction chance.",
  "675f67cb9d050e9f3e3de0f9 successMT": "See how bad that is for the gun? You gotta be careful what you're putting on, or taking off, your firearms.",
  "675f67cb9d050e9f3e3de0f9 acceptMT": "This thing is going to explode in my hands, I can just feel it...",

  "675f6876a6ab9d33f2b19446 name": "Those that never fail",
  "675f6876a6ab9d33f2b19446 description": "You know what's kinda funny? There are actually a few weapons in Tarkov that can't malfunction under any circumstance. The PPSH-41 is a shining example, but some other guns exist that will never break in this place. Go run around with them for a while as your final task.",
  "675f689463c10e73b4d9b3d0": "Kill 100 enemies with weapons that cannot suffer jams (PPSH, MP18, MP43, revolvers, and LMGs [except the RPK-16!])",
  "675f6876a6ab9d33f2b19446 successMT": "See? The accuracy decreases, sure, but they make great choices when you can't afford weapon repairs or just want to be sure that you can go for a long time with no issues.",
  "675f6876a6ab9d33f2b19446 acceptMT": "Even at 0 durability??? Noted...",

  "675f69113646a559a132025f name": "Noob tube!",
  "675f69113646a559a132025f description": "Underbarrel Grenade launchers are a fantastic, albiet it very expensive, way of getting a pretty free kill on an enemy. The impact explosion and propelled nature means no one is safe from an instant death. Have fun with this one!",
  "675f6929e01aef755c647205": "Kill 5 enemies with underbarrel grenade launchers.",
  "675f69113646a559a132025f successMT": "Boom! Those things are nasty, aren't they? Let's keep using them.",
  "675f69113646a559a132025f acceptMT": "Playing on easy mode today.",

  "675f6a0cbe1f4f9221e13f2f name": "Questionable countermeasures",
  "675f6a0cbe1f4f9221e13f2f description": "The sniper scavs are quite annoying, right? They're just always there, no matter how many times you've cleared that sniper nest, they're back every raid. I don't know what's up with death not affecting Tarkov like it should. On the bright side, killing is now quite morally ambiguous! Anyways, see if we can send somewhat of a message to them. Take out 10 of them with your grenade launcher.",
  "675f6a28715cc2bf5d0fc1a2": "Kill 5 sniper scavs with UBGLs",
  "675f6a0cbe1f4f9221e13f2f successMT": "You're getting pretty good at aiming with these things. Let's try even further out, alright?",
  "675f6a0cbe1f4f9221e13f2f acceptMT": "Seems a bit excessive, but I agree, they are annoying",

  "675f6a62b9f0aa454d32abb1 name": "Artillery strike",
  "675f6a62b9f0aa454d32abb1 description": "So, you've seem how the grenades are propelled, yes? You know what that means... they can go quite a long distance. I want 10 kills over 100 meters away. Aim very high.",
  "675f6a76bb03522a0bf473b2": "Kill 10 enemies over 60 meters away with UBGLs",
  "675f6a62b9f0aa454d32abb1 successMT": "Quite impressive! Those were really difficult shots, great aim.",
  "675f6a62b9f0aa454d32abb1 acceptMT": "Gonna need a ruler or something for this one.",

  "675f6970edd75c036dfa1116 name": "The bigger pipe",
  "675f6970edd75c036dfa1116 description": "I know the M32A1 isn't an UNDERBARREL grenade launcher, but it's a grenade launcher, ok? And it's what Mr. Big Pipe uses. You know how these go by now, you gotta do it with his own weapon. Go explode that guy straight to the next life, literally",
  "675f69c59c67a21c2b1f9a26": "Kill Big pipe with the M32A1 MSGL grenade launcher",
  "675f6970edd75c036dfa1116 successMT": "He's gonna take a while to respawn, that's for sure. Nice shot.",
  "675f6970edd75c036dfa1116 acceptMT": "Someone's getting blown up today. I really hope it's not me. I guess I'll just try again if it's me... weird how that works",

  "675f6b0e083bd1bdb1e05b69 name": "One man army",
  "675f6b0e083bd1bdb1e05b69 description": "You're gonna need a lot of grenades for this one. For your final challenge, I want you killing 8 enemies with your UBGL. ...You've already done more than that? Oh, silly! You have to do it in one raid! Enjoy!",
  "675f6b2067f6fbba7cc058f7": "Kill 8 enemies in one raid with UBGLs",
  "675f6b0e083bd1bdb1e05b69 successMT": "There's gonna be a lot of little bits lying around for a while... Good stuff, soldier.",
  "675f6b0e083bd1bdb1e05b69 acceptMT": "I mean... alright.",

  // Mental Quest Locales

  "675f6e2d337d5572765f2523 name": "Technically speaking",
  "675f6e2d337d5572765f2523 description": "Paying attention is quite important to one's survival. I will say, though, I don't understand why attention in tarkov seems relegated purely to looting containers... oh well, if that's what the kids want, that's what we'll give em. Let's start with some technical components. Wires, PC parts, all that jazz. Search the PC blocks for them.",
  "675f6e976ff06fd727ce4d7b": "Find a Bundle of wires",
  "675f6eaf5e0b8efc0b2cb559": "Find some Capacitors",
  "675f6ebc6b4cfc71888e9ed5": "Find a DVD drive",
  "675f6ec26b5dc04f08bfe62b": "Find an HDD drive",
  "675f6ec96f7be8b959ddad75": "Find a CPU fan",
  "675f6ecf13651b8eeb3b8917": "Find some Electronical Components",
  "675f6ed5e090619b2e3cfeec": "Find an ES lamp",
  "675f6eda9c24dc3da1b54411": "Find a UV lamp",
  "675f6edec521f8943ba3fcaf": "Find a PC CPU",
  "675f6ee3d9df4fc1f89133db": "Find a Power cord",
  "675f6e2d337d5572765f2523 successMT": "Nice! You could build your own pc with all those parts",
  "675f6e2d337d5572765f2523 acceptMT": "This sets a bad precedent...",

  "675f6efb8c8f84c13f1c2d24 name": "Filling the toolbox",
  "675f6efb8c8f84c13f1c2d24 description": "You've got a lot of technical components lying around, but you can't just smash them together with your bare hands. You need some tools. Go loot the toolboxes around tarkov to fill your own",
  "675f6f6313b23217b33c244a": "Find an awl",
  "675f6f6cb4a167ff3a75e6a5": "Find a cable cutter",
  "675f6f76d40b48b8ca7d4d82": "Find some measuring tape",
  "675f6f7f019ecee9f7348043": "Find an eletric drill",
  "675f6f88bbbe2dac0ca61739": "Find a sledgehammer",
  "675f6f96016920771641b322": "Find a flat screwdriver",
  "675f6fa04116811338b7f627": "Find a long & flat screwdriver",
  "675f6fa607965bf4cfd46cfc": "Find a hand drill",
  "675f6fae08b6e4f918735725": "Find some metal cutting scissors",
  "675f6fb6e7eb0cdf3eab90d1": "Find some nippers",
  "675f6fbdd5dc0ce431ee59ca": "Find an old firesteel",
  "675f6fc3398eb2549359d5e4": "Find a pipe grip wrench",
  "675f701d8a67ab75d3fa64a7": "Find some pliers",
  "675f70255cefac2c6e6fc6e0": "Find some elite pliers",
  "675f702beaae1c9c4b7e4695": "Find a ratchet wrench",
  "675f7030d4e9108dd60c1a7b": "Find some round pliers",
  "675f7038c410334b565de95f": "Find a screwdriver",
  "675f704009cd39fd1ecb07da": "Find a set of 'Master' files",
  "675f7049708fbc612adabf4b": "Find a sewing kit",
  "675f7051291813e52bb04c07": "Find a wrench",
  "675f6efb8c8f84c13f1c2d24 successMT": "That's gotta be a heavy toolbox at that point. I hope you've been levelling your strength a bit.",
  "675f6efb8c8f84c13f1c2d24 acceptMT": "What's a man without his tools?",

  "675f70cbabb1b13ec6bb1d9f name": "Stockpile",
  "675f70cbabb1b13ec6bb1d9f description": "All these tools and eletronical pieces are nice, but they won't really help you in a gunfight, will they? You need something more practical. Parts won't always solve a debate... bullets will. Hmmm... perhaps some packaged rounds will do you good? Better chance they aren't tampered with.",
  "675f70ed48a3a8d2a54fd992": "Collect 25 boxes of ammo (don't open them!)",
  "675f70cbabb1b13ec6bb1d9f successMT": "How many different calibers can you service with all that? The nice thing about this, as well, is that it's free. No need to spend thousands of roubles on these.",
  "675f70cbabb1b13ec6bb1d9f acceptMT": "I won't complain about more ammo. That's a lot, though.",

  "675f7158036c206f933eb5ff name": "Rare catch",
  "675f7158036c206f933eb5ff description": "Some items in Tarkov seem so expensive, don't they? Millions of roubles for one little device? That's the law of supply and demand in action. Why spend millions when you can spend a few minutes just finding the item yourself? You know, 15 minutes could save you 15% or more on-",
  "675f716755bda671d25734ac": "Find an Iridium",
  "675f7176929bad06f9ef8441": "Find a Folder With Intelligence",
  "675f717da4d6bbefc25291f0": "Find a GPU",
  "675f719fe36ce29758861874": "Find a Tetriz",
  "675f71a464ad0da5dc955312": "Find a LEDX",
  "675f71ada08160790b189921": "Find a Defibrillator",
  "675f7158036c206f933eb5ff successMT": "How exactly does this relate to attention? I don't know, ask BattleState Games. Erm, I mean, ask Terragroup. Yeah, ask Terragroup. They caused all this. Heh.",
  "675f7158036c206f933eb5ff acceptMT": "There's no way a celestial being just hit me with a Geico ad. What on earth is this thing?",

  "Rewrite this": "We need to re-write most of the quests in this section. How fun!",
  "Nevermind": "Turns out we only adjusted a couple Charisma quests. Nice!",
  "Nevermind times two": "Actually, we redid some of Attention to work better, as well as AD3. Oh well!",

  "675f7b5dead60ebf17c84cef name": "Getting familiar",
  "675f7b5dead60ebf17c84cef description": "If you're going to be here a while, you should get to know all the big figures around here. Maybe help them out, unlock some stuff for yourself.",
  "675f7bab86f12c50cbd91d26": "Prapor LL2",
  "675f7bb1d68ec8c97f2704e8": "Therapist LL2",
  "675f7d51251a073a3f7a515a": "Skier LL2",
  "675f7d58d8b0489fe9befc60": "Peacekeeper LL2",
  "675f7d5ea3027aa26d5c6f14": "Mechanic LL2",
  "675f7d657cb0f6e8e698199b": "Ragman LL2",
  "675f7d6d29905f0f12452f39": "Jaeger LL2",
  "675f7b5dead60ebf17c84cef successMT": "Good, glad to see you making some allies. Surviving alone is difficult, after all",
  "675f7b5dead60ebf17c84cef acceptMT": "What if I don't want to do Jaeger quests?",

  "675f7d83ee2ed3915390aaae name": "Acquiring capital",
  "675f7d83ee2ed3915390aaae description": "Now that you've gotten to know some people, you should make sure you can actually trade with them. You have some money by now, don't you?",
  "675f7d97c95a980dee2d7ffd": "Acquire 1000000 roubles",
  "675f7dbf6362f8e8123b3076": "Acquire 6000 euros",
  "675f7dc4314cc77c6a1ab75b": "Acquire 6500 dollars",
  "675f7d83ee2ed3915390aaae successMT": "Oh, good! You're not broke. Money is critical to survival, even if we wish it wasn't.",
  "675f7d83ee2ed3915390aaae acceptMT": "It always wraps back around to money, doesn't it...",

  "675f7dec7b1039cf247e80f1 name": "Purchasing equipment",
  "675f7dec7b1039cf247e80f1 description": "You've got the cash, you've got some allies, and they would love to sell to you. Guns, medicine, cases, so many things. Why not take advantage of this?",
  "675f7e4a1446dd6d6732e9d9": "Spend a total of 2 million currency on trades (USD and EUR convert to roubles)",
  "675f7e5a31f37617883a8a1c": "Spend ₽1M roubles",
  "675f7e6226594452c48ff739": "Spend €6K Euros",
  "675f7e678c504ce7f893397e": "Spend $6.5K USD",
  "675f7dec7b1039cf247e80f1 successMT": "Earning cash, spending cash, earning more cash... what a cycle. *sigh*. Makes you ",
  "675f7dec7b1039cf247e80f1 acceptMT": "I'm telling you, I don't want to work with this Jaeger guy, he makes me do weird stuff",

  "675f7ea44dbf005c30fcee17 name": "Breaking the bank",
  "675f7ea44dbf005c30fcee17 description": "So much money... where's all this stuff coming from anyways? I guess things keep respawning, so there's infinite wealth as long as you hang around. Well, lets push it to the limit.",
  "6a0c018c2f158ea67c6f1a2f": "Spend a total of 30 million currency on trades (USD and EUR convert to roubles)",
  "6a0c01b52f158ea67c6f1a30": "Earn a total of 15 million currency from trades (USD and EUR convert to roubles)",
  "675f7ea44dbf005c30fcee17 successMT": "My, my! Seems like all the traders can't stop talking about you. And to see how much you've done with me is quite impressive.",
  "675f7ea44dbf005c30fcee17 acceptMT": "How exactly am I meant to 'understand' a celestial being?",

  "675f7f7a5aa154ae19f5a82a name": "The test begins",
  "675f7f7a5aa154ae19f5a82a description": "'Light, how are you supposed to train my intelligence? Are you going to have me read books or something?' Hahaha... that's a good idea, actually. But no, I have something much more exciting for you. Riddles! Oh yes, I'm serious. We'll begin easily. Prapor once had a friend, a friend he wouldn't tell you about unless you wacked some scavs. Or used your intelligence center to look it up. Don't do that here, by the way. You'll ruin the fun. Anyways, where did this friend live?",
  "675f7f96ece57c78a18641c5": "Locate the spot of the riddle",
  "675f7f7a5aa154ae19f5a82a successMT": "He was a good friend, so I've heard.",
  "675f7f7a5aa154ae19f5a82a acceptMT": "I enjoyed killing the scavs, by the way",

  "675f7fc218ad814cbf690c1f name": "Thirsting for more",
  "675f7fc218ad814cbf690c1f description": "There is something all humans need to live, more frequently than food, but less frequently than air. Somewhere, there is a large stash that one of your 'traders' took interest in. Where was this?",
  "675f7fdb6151781b3403040f": "Locate the spot of the riddle",
  "675f7fc218ad814cbf690c1f successMT": "Nice! Don't forget to stay hydrated, while you're at it.",
  "675f7fc218ad814cbf690c1f acceptMT": "Are riddles customary with this thing?",

  "675f8008b7831ecb4e5db0e7 name": "Raising the stakes",
  "675f8008b7831ecb4e5db0e7 description": "Alright, lets make things more difficult: In war, rarely is there a 'good' side. Sometimes, fighting for either side is wrong. Sometimes, fighting for either side is right. Sometimes, you get a choice which side you'll fight for. Sometimes, mass life or death hangs in the balance of one small thing: Who you tell. Do you do what is right? Is there a 'right?' Or do you tell the one who gives you the rewards you seek?",
  "675f8024e38f2dd530cea750": "Locate the spot of the riddle",
  "675f8008b7831ecb4e5db0e7 successMT": "I am curious, who did you end up telling?",
  "675f8008b7831ecb4e5db0e7 acceptMT": "I choose what I'll use most, probably.",

  "682fdbb4680f61b0ed38d3a5 name": "Bonus quest (Intelligence): 6 lies and a truth.",
  "682fdbb4680f61b0ed38d3a5 description": "I had a fun idea, as a test of your current intelligence. Are you able to identify differneces between what seems to be identical things? If I were to give you the same quest 7 times, but only one was the 'true' one, would you be able to figure it out? There's no penalty for failure, but you will be rewarded if you succeed. You only get one try, though, so take your time!",
  "682fdbbb326f0e39e7dda82e": "Completing this will create 7 'quests'.",
  "682fdbb4680f61b0ed38d3a5 successMT": "Alright, good look! Remember, you only get one shot. Turn in the correct one!",
  "682fdbb4680f61b0ed38d3a5 acceptMT": "Oh lord.",

  "675f80b4625238051edb9d0e name": "Nearing the end",
  "675f80b4625238051edb9d0e description": "In a place created for creation, where the hammer falls on the unforged and unfortunate, a crash is heard in the dead of night. Black grains in blue packages are hidden, and the one who mends the biological has paid the one who mends the material. Tell me, where were the black grains laid?",
  "675f80cd33dd203e0f69b360": "Locate the spot of the riddle",
  "675f80b4625238051edb9d0e successMT": "That was a tough one, eh? Will the last one be tougher, or easier? I suppose it depends on how well you know your stuff.",
  "675f80b4625238051edb9d0e acceptMT": "No hints for the hard ones!",

  "675f811444410a14d5c5f85f name": "The final riddle",
  "675f811444410a14d5c5f85f description": "Last one... let's make it difficult: Near the open sea, where the fish swam and the birds flew freely, Contract wars were waged. The sea, once cared for, now laps silently on the beach, and the wings no longer fly undisturbed. One bird, however, was determined to fly, but the eagles consumed the bird's attempt. Where does this bird lie?",
  "675f81330700ccbf45fa101e": "Locate the spot of the riddle",
  "675f811444410a14d5c5f85f successMT": "Well done! You really know how to think. Or you happened upon it by accident, in which case, booooo. Oh well. You made it this far, good job.",
  "675f811444410a14d5c5f85f acceptMT": "No hints for the hard ones!",

  "675f815853dc84fb72dc812e name": "Changing the rules",
  "675f815853dc84fb72dc812e description": "Look, I know that you pmcs normally train your perception by looting things, and that's fine. But I think we're both getting tired of just picking up items. I have you doing that enough for Attention and Search. So, let's do something more exciting for this one, alright? We'll work on hearing things and spotting things. First, let's do some spotting. Take out some enemies at medium range, lets say, 50m or longer.",
  "675f8171966ba88b201accd9": "Kill 8 enemies at 50+ meters",
  "675f815853dc84fb72dc812e successMT": "Got a pretty good pair of eyes, eh? If only they could perceive the divine... oh well.",
  "675f815853dc84fb72dc812e acceptMT": "I suppose it's a nice change of pace.",

  "675f81b15de9c5a71442fe8d name": "Tuning the audio",
  "675f81b15de9c5a71442fe8d description": "Killing an enemy at long range ensures they never even hear you. But, you don't get to hear them either. Sometimes, there is no choice of long-range. You need to know how to out-hear your enemies.",
  "675f81e320b59a5501c5f994": "Kill 3 enemies with the GSSh-01 headset",
  "675f81e89ef8976c0a0c2985": "Kill 3 enemies with the MSA Sordin headset",
  "675f8200adf980e5a89e6304": "Kill 3 enemies with the FAST RAC headset",
  "675f8204d82923d76ad025c1": "Kill 3 enemies with the Earmor M32 headset",
  "675f821ca912fc7ccf7c4427": "Kill 3 enemies with the Comtac 2 headset",
  "675f8223563b3e21b4ee1e48": "Kill 3 enemies with the Comtac 4",
  "675f823cda12ae7cd2a8ae64": "Kill 3 enemies with the Tactical Sport",
  "675f8243bc1d35d3fa843a77": "Kill 3 enemies with the Razor Digital headset",
  "675f825a1cc2443f79e12e32": "Kill 3 enemies with the XCEL 500BT",
  "675f825f069040cbfd49e834": "ALL KILLS MUST BE WITHIN 40 METERS",
  "675f81b15de9c5a71442fe8d successMT": "So, which headset did you like best? Could you tell the difference between each one, or did some feel the same?",
  "675f81b15de9c5a71442fe8d acceptMT": "This one might actually benefit me",

  "675f828cd042843bfc741215 name": "Noise cancellation",
  "675f828cd042843bfc741215 description": "We just went and tested all the headsets avaliable in Tarkov. Now, let's see how you fair with the opposite: Sound reduction. Heavy helmets are great for blocking a few rounds, especially from most scavs, but they also block your hearing. Will you fair just as well?",
  "675f82a8074a284d2b41db49": "Kill 20 enemies within 50 meters while wearing a helmet with high sound reduction (check wiki for list)",
  "675f828cd042843bfc741215 successMT": "What do you think? Do you prefer the protection, or the hearing? Personally, I prefer the hearing. But then again, I need no protection where I'm at. The louder I can hear Him, the better.",
  "675f828cd042843bfc741215 acceptMT": "Is this a blessing or a curse?",

  "675f82bc04bbb9e015a6dbcb name": "Shot of the century",
  "675f82bc04bbb9e015a6dbcb description": "I think your hearing is just fine, let's conclude with something satisfying. You got some kills a medium distance a while ago, remember? But with scopes, even long distance can look like point blank range. So here's a challenge: I want you to kill someone that's further than 150 meters away from you. With only iron sights. Yep, no scopes, no reflex sights, no cheating by having iron sights equipped and welding a dovetail on the sight, just pure iron sights. Have fun!",
  "675f82d79df4f6b630b1763d": "Headshot an enemy over 150m away with iron sights.",
  "675f82bc04bbb9e015a6dbcb successMT": "Wow. Just wow. I don't say this often, but I seriously wasn't expecting that. That's got to be the shot of the century or something.",
  "675f82bc04bbb9e015a6dbcb acceptMT": "Well, screw me I guess",

  //Physical Quest Locales
  "675f85992e1f423a9e81192a name": "The human will to live",
  "675f85992e1f423a9e81192a description": "Endurance, perserverance... hmm... well ",
  "675f85e9bd133fd7cf040045": "Survive 3 raids in a row (run through does not count, but won't reset)",
  "675f85992e1f423a9e81192a successMT": "Look at that, you can survive for more than 20 minutes!",
  "675f85992e1f423a9e81192a acceptMT": "Oh that's nice, the angel actually wants me to live.",

  "675f868cb5bc94b6c1d67760 name": "Marathon",
  "675f868cb5bc94b6c1d67760 description": "Some people just like watching counters go up. Kinda weird, isn't it? I don't quite get it, I think work is best when you can't see the results so obviously, or track it so meticulously. Well, that's what I'm having you do this time, I suppose. The good news is this one is easy! Just run around a lot.",
  "6806a7fe7e972c54679d86b0": "Move 42195 meters",
  "6806b780b28dbaddba66d736": "Move 500 meters in the Factory",
  "6806b7b5709a49af590d167a": "Move 1000 meters on Interchange",
  "6806b7e884da7a603b478079": "Move 1000 meters on Customs",
  "6806b7f769c6e31fc5e78c85": "Move 1000 meters on Streets",
  "6806b804c09e52e76f448edc": "Move 1000 meters on Reserve",
  "6806b83082a28fdf28ae26dd": "Move 1000 meters on Lighthouse",
  "6806b837be1ffe9ccfe27c7b": "Move 1000 meters on Shoreline",
  "6806b86455e6155bb61cf0af": "Move 1000 meters on Ground Zero",
  "6806b87c56ff93e220633f2d": "Move 1000 meters on Woods",
  "6806b88db41940e6827a3537": "Move 500 meters in The Lab",
  "675f868cb5bc94b6c1d67760 successMT": "Is Tarkov not a lovely place? I mean, everyone's killing each other, that ruins the tourism a bit. Or does it? You're here, haha. Anyways, it's a shame what happened. The beaches of Shoreline and Lighthouse, the shopping mall, the streets... so much destruction. Have you ever wondered if you could stop it, or are you only concerned about escaping?",
  "675f868cb5bc94b6c1d67760 acceptMT": "WHY?!? WHYYYYYY",

  "675f87672fdf376c5984a137 name": "A life well spent",
  "675f87672fdf376c5984a137 description": "What to do with your last endurance task... hmm... I suppose just 'enduring' in general works. Sound good? Alright, go get 100 of them, without dying. They can't only be scavs, by the way.",
  "675f878e27ecb05716fc2736": "Kill 100 enemies without dying",
  "675f879a50fa8cd23d8be4fd": "15 of them being PMCs",
  "675f87a712fb1f1f0c56b6ad": "3 of them being bosses (Each goon counts, but other guards don't)",
  "675f87672fdf376c5984a137 successMT": "Well, well... been a while since you died. What a mess you've made, though... eh, it all seems to reset anyways.",
  "675f87672fdf376c5984a137 acceptMT": "Oh.",

  "675f88580b54938c23315549 name": "Are you feeling it now?",
  "675f88580b54938c23315549 description": "What does it even mean to have 'health 0'? Whatever, let's fix that. I'm sure you've noticed that certain things happen to you sometimes when you're in combat. What happens if you're under an effect for a long time? Maybe you're looping painkillers, or you've got something you can't fix. Who knows?",
  "675f8879cf1342909190bf15": "Have any status effect for 10 minutes",
  "675f88580b54938c23315549 successMT": "So, did you survive? Either way, I can see your body preparing for that situation again. You're getting 'healthier' or something. What? I'm not a doctor, I'm an angel. The human understanding of medicine confuses me anyways. It's seen as so important and lifesaving, yet you hide it behind massive paywalls? Whatever happened to caring for the sick and needy? *sigh*... I'm getting off topic. Make sure you complete your other physical trainings.",
  "675f88580b54938c23315549 acceptMT": "I don't think this will feel good",

  "675f88dd535b7935e148a19d name": "Medical Master",
  "675f88dd535b7935e148a19d description": "Having a bunch of health effects is one thing. Do you know how to treat them? What do you do when you've been shot, arms broken, insides spilling outward? I mean, sure, you just die and come back, you always do. But what if you didn't die? Show me that you know how to use medicine. I do not care what kind of medicine, use whatever you fancy. Just make sure all your bases are covered.",
  "675f88fe1cf0f108fd43dfe3": "Use any medical item (including stims) a total of 300 times",
  "68069869c884e16e737d6622": "Fix 15 bleeds",
  "680699ab7e34f09f5d5108e8": "Fix 5 fractures",
  "675f88dd535b7935e148a19d successMT": "You clearly know how to take care of yourself and respond to crisis. Good, good!",
  "675f88dd535b7935e148a19d acceptMT": "Wait, doesn't this require me getting hurt a lot?",

  "675f89308ea18c3061b5d16d name": "Unmatched Physique",
  "675f89308ea18c3061b5d16d description": "What is health by itself? Can you even be considered healthy if you can Endure nothing, if you have not the Strength to carry on? It's Stressful to think of not taking care of such Vital skills... ironic, considering I have full Immunity. Anyways, show me that you have properly Metabolized what you have been trained so far.",
  "675f897b40d2d82feaa1124a": "Reach Endurance level 30",
  "675f897422cd3bbfedafce63": "Reach Immunity level 15",
  "675f896d0216e6c277b1b867": "Reach Metabolism level 50",
  "675f89660462c7e31634cf30": "Reach Strength level 30",
  "675f8961e9eef4dfffe2129b": "Reach Stress Resistance level 20",
  "675f895c8e49e39e992db2ff": "Reach Vitality level 20",
  "675f89308ea18c3061b5d16d successMT": "Sheeeeeesh... you're the embodiment of health now, super soldier. Feels good, doesn't it? Feels like you can do anything. Just don't forget about the One who can truly do all things. Talk about being made in His image, though.",
  "675f89308ea18c3061b5d16d acceptMT": "Looks like I need to become a master of all trades",

  "675f89bdd76e3d5909062966 name": "Researching",
  "675f89bdd76e3d5909062966 description": "I've heard a bit about biological warfare being used down there, but I'm not sure what exactly it is. I'm sure you've heard more, being down there in the middle of it. Can you acquire whatever instrument is being used to 'deliver' this toxin? If you know anything about a cure for it, I'd like to see that as well.",
  "675f89d795d38eebb1d83844": "Hand over a cultist knife",
  "675f89dd8088abecc187c2bd": "Hand over an antidote ",
  "675f89bdd76e3d5909062966 successMT": "Were you able to get a fresh one? Ah, no worries, this stuff seems dangerous. I'll do some researching and find out what this is. Oh, you can keep the knife and antidote. I can't exactly take it from you, remember?",
  "675f89bdd76e3d5909062966 acceptMT": "Maybe I should get these off a buyer... I don't think I want to risk being stabbed",

  "675f8a4928af96343171dd98 name": "Unethical Testing",
  "675f8a4928af96343171dd98 description": "I've seen quite a lot of drugs show up in Tarkov recently, seems like Terragroup was busy in their experiments. I have a favor to ask... you wouldn't mind seeing what they do, would you? Y'know, empirically? You'll be fine, I think.",
  "675f8aa002f7f1473e8923ea": "Use Meldonin",
  "675f8aade3f5a07308289662": "Use 3-(b-TG)",
  "675f8ab99982c5128d9fca1a": "Use SJ9",
  "675f8ac80a4bd5d67f6c2c15": "Use SJ12",
  "675f8ad5517311ce6fe4d977": "Use L1",
  "675f8ae3dd72a7de2247f376": "Use P22",
  "675f8aee8de9afc1aad81091": "Use Obdolbos",
  "675f8af2b47701adf88e41cf": "Use Obdolbos2",
  "675f8b02a72064c099d786e2": "Use PNB",
  "675f8b078802842ec5799d2c": "Use Perfotoran",
  "675f8b1959f3b862d7f7748c": "Use Trimodal",
  "675f8b20b44148c285164c16": "Use xtg-12",
  "675f8a4928af96343171dd98 successMT": "Interesting, so that's what they all do... the human history division of heaven thanks you for your literal sacrifice.",
  "675f8a4928af96343171dd98 acceptMT": "Great, I'm sure nothing can go wrong with this...",

  "675f8b391637a6131f7e3d73 name": "Knowing the professionals",
  "675f8b391637a6131f7e3d73 description": "I feel a little bad about what I asked you to do last time... maybe we should just stick to the people that know about this. You have a medical professional here, correct?",
  "675f8b92a4ef04670ff268eb": "Reach LL4 Therapist",
  "675f8b391637a6131f7e3d73 successMT": "So you do! Good, I don't think we'll need to do any more experiments with your body from now on. Sorry about that!",
  "675f8b391637a6131f7e3d73 acceptMT": "Why didn't we start with this idea?",

  "675f8bfe9a64a2163df07856 name": "Immunity through extermination",
  "675f8bfe9a64a2163df07856 description": "Your immune system has gotten a lot stronger through all this! However, it's not the type of thing you 'want' to put to the test. So, let's eliminate the source of the toxin, shall we? Or, more accurately, eliminate those who seek to weaponize it. Those cultists interfere with my work anyways, worshipping whatever satanic deity they do. It probably is satan himself, from what I've seen of them. Two birds with one stone, eh? ",
  "675f8c106c0d0a122f9d7e97": "Kill 25 cultists",
  "675f8bfe9a64a2163df07856 successMT": "I'd love to say something like 'good job, you really messed them up!' but that didn't even leave a mark on their prescence. They're talking about you know, and seek your painful death, but that's about it. There will always be worshippers of evil, I suppose... I fear how many we see nowadays. Makes me thing the Lord's coming back is soon. Oh well. I'll let you know what we should do next.",
  "675f8bfe9a64a2163df07856 acceptMT": "I don't think this is how immunity works.",

  "675f8c40c1386be2ce870b07 name": "Ultimate Innoculation",
  "675f8c40c1386be2ce870b07 description": "Hey, so... I know I've said a lot about how we're not going to run experiments on your body anymore, and I meant that. I'm sorry in advance for what I have to ask of you next. You see, when a pathogen is in your body that your body doesn't like, it creates antibodies to fight it off. It also keeps a 'record' of the pathogen to be able to fight it off more effectively. The reason people keep getting sick from the 'same' sickness is because it mutates. However, I've noticed that whatever toxin those cultists have created, there's only one strain. It's one specific poison. ...I'm going to judge by the look on your face that you've figured out where this is going. I'm sorry, friend. 5 minutes should be long enough for your body to get enough information on it. Keep yourself alive, alright?",
  "675f8c58b2280ff073b65129": "Survive a posioning for five minutes",
  "675f8c40c1386be2ce870b07 successMT": "Did it work? Oh, praise the Lord! You've built up a serious resistance to the pathogen by doing that, it should never be that bad again. It looks like you had strengthed your immune system enough before this that it had a much easier time fighting that. Did I mention you're the first person to survive that? Well done, well done! Celebrate with a few more cultist deaths for me, will ya? Hahahaha!!!",
  "675f8c40c1386be2ce870b07 acceptMT": "Am I seriously going through with this? This is going to be the most painful thing I've ever experienced.",

  "675f8ce0c8d7be6b6bc62677 name": "Running on fumes",
  "675f8ce0c8d7be6b6bc62677 description": "You know those moments where you are just so exhausted, so low on energy, but you've gotta push just a liiiiittle bit longer? Yeah, that can happen in combat too. Will you be capable of shooting straight when you've got almost nothing left?",
  "675f8d0ccd765e50d36fd931": "Kill an enemy while suffering from either exhaustion and dehydration",
  "675f8ce0c8d7be6b6bc62677 successMT": "So you can! Seems like there's nothing you can't do. Although, you have unlimited attempts, haha.",
  "675f8ce0c8d7be6b6bc62677 acceptMT": "This angel is starting to seem like the ghost of Jaeger future...",

  "675f8d2a30cca3c591eb2374 name": "Infinite Palate",
  "675f8d2a30cca3c591eb2374 description": "What was your favorite thing to eat before you got here? Is it something you could still find? I guess you don't get much choice about it anymore. You have to eat whatever you come across, don't you. You can eat anything, right? Except the mayo. Don't eat the mayo. That's just gross.",
  "675f8d584eb09a29526adc93": "Consume an Alyonka",
  "675f8d636cd6f180c91e2fce": "Consume an Aquamari",
  "675f8d6fef29109fa4ba809e": "Consume some crackers",
  "675f8d7cb2569574f812f1e1": "Consume a Kvass",
  "675f8d81d0d3a2faa63f8d30": "Consume some Whiskey",
  "675f8d9277b21a9dce201c6d": "Consume some of the good stuff (Moonshine)",
  "675f8d9ce59ff763c62776ef": "Consume some light beer",
  "675f8da9c7270e6b13d8d219": "Consume some vodka",
  "675f8db58002b9ef5f478cb3": "Consume a bottle of water",
  "675f8dc094f635750fb566d2": "Consume a beef stew",
  "675f8dc64a4b15a29c148e3a": "Consume a beef stew, but smol",
  "675f8debc18d7c4b3322179c": "Consume some condensed milk",
  "675f8df0f988314941aec4c9": "Consume some peas",
  "675f8e0a994c35fb45278900": "Consume some herring",
  "675f8e12d76f78015497ea81": "Consume a car",
  "675f8e1d5b09ed4950f56988": "Consume the salmon",
  "675f8e30c7f98a23b75ade2c": "Consume some tea",
  "675f8e4157fea3a5e2ee4993": "Consume the maximum energy drink",
  "675f8e470f331552551726fa": "Consume the saury",
  "675f8e5b5a87faf32575fd61": "Consume the Rat",
  "675f8e678eae79d73fa67aad": "Consume some sprats",
  "675f8e77c7a4d400a3ad927f": "Consume some squash (ew)",
  "675f8e86d127ff8be11b6125": "Consume soda",
  "675f8e91aea4e323fe1d76cc": "Consume a whole lot of water. Seriously how do you drink that in one go",
  "675f8ea109b9b65e6336eae0": "Consume Emelya",
  "675f8eac543aea3f1ba2df44": "Consume EWR",
  "675f8eb7165c80ce3c33404c": "Consume the Russain rations",
  "675f8ec22bbbe51ca2ddfb5f": "Consume the American rations",
  "675f8ecd5ba2813602ad55e8": "Consume an apple juice",
  "675f8ed8f6f30870592871e8": "Consume some grapefruit juice",
  "675f8ee42e2aaa1ffddfd85a": "Consume some milk (it's probably spoiled)",
  "675f8ef1c0fcc244bd2e2571": "Consume some oat flakes",
  "675f8efcd69a8ba66b1d098b": "Consume some pineapple juice",
  "675f8f0b943bdbae721d3ee5": "Consume some sugar",
  "675f8f15215e7f17b7fb5758": "Consume some multivitamin juice",
  "675f8f3b9af707a14799f478": "Consume some normal croutons",
  "675f8f457d9b23966a358e38": "Consume the delicous sausage",
  "675f8f52d16bea9772c371f5": "Consume the off-brand chocolate (Slickers)",
  "675f8cd434bc0d5a81f19723": "Consume a college student's meal (Instant noodles)",
  "675f8ccad9df021a32fbbf19": "Consume some quality jerky",
  "675f8d2a30cca3c591eb2374 successMT": "Wow, you really can eat anything you find. That's probably healthy? Not being picky helps you survive, but being picky can also be a survival instinct.",
  "675f8d2a30cca3c591eb2374 acceptMT": "I might gain some weight doing this",

  "675f8f9ac46b5dcd9037c0b6 name": "Deadlift",
  "675f8f9ac46b5dcd9037c0b6 description": "A major sign of strength is lifting, right? I never quite understood what's so cool about it, but I suppose it has some advantages. Being able to drag your buddies out of fire, for example. Well, anyways, let's see where you are at the moment.",
  "675f8fb4479687ba7e7b187e": "Achieve critical overweight in raid.",
  "675f8f9ac46b5dcd9037c0b6 successMT": "Found your limit? The good news is that it can only go up from here. Keep working!",
  "675f8f9ac46b5dcd9037c0b6 acceptMT": "Is this a fight for my life, or a game of football?",

  "675f8fd8f0705b9c4f6ff3ab name": "Parkour",
  "675f8fd8f0705b9c4f6ff3ab description": "Look at you, putting on some muscle! I have a fun idea for you, a way to jump around like a little kid again. You see, there's a couple spots that require a certain 'strength level' to reach. Do you think you're there yet? Or do you need a while longer? Oh, and don't worry. IncreasedClimbHeight won't help you here. Uhm, you probably want a lighter kit as well... (TESTED AT STRENGTH 15 WHILE NOT OVERWEIGHT)",
  "675f8ff578cbfa58e6860206": "Reach the top of the yellow bus in Scav Town on Woods",
  "675f9003592e6db90b93b5da": "Reach the ladder on the red container of the scav tower on Woods",
  "675f900eda20cc8b127c810d": "Reach the top of container/house 44 in the storage area on Customs ",
  "675f901a80aa96065737bcb2": "Reach the top of the left fuel tank in the row of 4 fuel tanks near construction on Customs",
  "675f8fd8f0705b9c4f6ff3ab successMT": "How about that? You made it there in the end. Good job, Mr. Monkey. The last challenge won't be so pretty.",
  "675f8fd8f0705b9c4f6ff3ab acceptMT": "Not the strangest thing you'll ask me to do, is it?",

  "675f90b6411b4db706023982 name": "Gladiator",
  "675f90b6411b4db706023982 description": "Alright, you want a really challenge? Those bosses around Tarkov, they seem pretty tough. Most got guards or heavy armour, better accuracy, more health... how does more health even work anyways? Ah well, you're gonna knock one down big time. Pick your favorite one around tarkov, and kill him with a melee weapon. Feel free to weaken him with bullets if you must, I'd recommend a flashbang as well, but the killing blow has to come from a melee weapon. Let's see you prove your strength.",
  "675f90cf97932a5d4c5f3472": "Kill a boss with a melee weapon and survive the raid.",
  "675f90b6411b4db706023982 successMT": "That look on your face... ...you enjoyed that, didn't you?",
  "675f90b6411b4db706023982 acceptMT": "Nothing personal, kid",

  "675f91b9d584742a5a2e4d70 name": "No pain, no gain",
  "675f91b9d584742a5a2e4d70 description": "Pain is a hard sensation to override. It seizes control of you, it makes you want to curl up and hold the afflicted area tightly. Unfortunately, you find yourself in a situation where that will only lead to more pain, and then death. Well, whatever death means to you. It's bad regardless, so you need to learn to fight that sensation off.",
  "675f91ea011e963c77ac4fa8": "Kill five enemies while suffering pain",
  "675f91b9d584742a5a2e4d70 successMT": "You barely flinched, and those were some gnarly wounds! You've defintiely got your pain receptors under control. But there's more than just some subcutaneous stimulators to worry about, let us continue.",
  "675f91b9d584742a5a2e4d70 acceptMT": "But why?",

  "675f92428204b0ff6d723f0b name": "Dazzled, not deterred",
  "675f92428204b0ff6d723f0b description": "You can override your pain, and that's important. But what happens when you can't override something? You can't override a stun grenade thourgh sheer willpower. Or can you? Perhaps you can fight through it? I don't know, you show me.",
  "675f928eff18b8cf41987088": "Kill three enemies while suffering contusion or stunned",
  "675f92428204b0ff6d723f0b successMT": "That was a stunning performance! .....anyways, you really suprised me there. I thought a stun grenade was the end of a fight, but you proved that nothing can prevent you from killing. Hmmm... is that a bad thing?",
  "675f92428204b0ff6d723f0b acceptMT": "BUT WHY?",

  "675f92bbebff7cef92ec8584 name": "Wounds heal",
  "675f92bbebff7cef92ec8584 description": "You have to be careful with a fresh wound. It can get infected, it can start bleeding again, it can swell, there's a whole lot of things that can go on. They heal over time, though. The human body has amazing regenerative capabilities. However, no one in Tarkov is going to wait a few days for you to 'get well'. It's only something to take advantage of here. Show them that you don't need to wait.",
  "675f92da5fb3c0e8b1f8cd5c": "Kill 30 enemies while having a fresh wound",
  "675f92bbebff7cef92ec8584 successMT": "I can read your thoughts, by the way. I'm not sadistic, this isn't a pleasure for me. I'm here to train you to survive in Tarkov for a greater purpose. I understand why you feel that way though, I hope you can forgive me. I have one more thing to ask of you, anyways. Oh, and good job surviving out there while wounded. Getting beat up does not make it any easier to fight back",
  "675f92bbebff7cef92ec8584 acceptMT": "I'm starting to think this thing is a sadist",

  "675f92fd0f975501f7ab1de4 name": "Current objective: KILL",
  "675f92fd0f975501f7ab1de4 description": "So far, I've been testing your ability to handle individual things. Pain, blindness, severe wounds. For your final test, we'll do something different, perhaps something more enjoyable. Let's see how you do against a horde of people coming after you!",
  "675f9325c25d93710c7e7cd4": "Complete either of the options in one raid and survive",
  "682d7646f9d966793e9579b6": "Kill 25 enemies",
  "682d7644f5e1d514de782e7c": "Deal 5000 damage",
  "675f92fd0f975501f7ab1de4 successMT": "So much blood in such a short time... and you look like you had fun. Horrifying. Go on, then; I don't think anything will stress you out.",
  "675f92fd0f975501f7ab1de4 acceptMT": "A different kind of stress...",

  "675f93f1d40d1e0ee8bc1b25 name": "No time to bleed",
  "675f93f1d40d1e0ee8bc1b25 description": "You wanna hear something painfully obvious? Bleeding isn't good. Yet there sure as heck seems to be a lot of blood spilled in this region. I'm actually not great with blood myself... I don't get sick or anything, I just dislike seeing it except for very specific circumstances. Do me a favor, keep your blood inside your body. I think it'd appreciate it as well.",
  "675f940f522626bacfc3cd13": "Stop 7 bleeds",
  "675f93f1d40d1e0ee8bc1b25 successMT": "Good! I'm glad to see that you know how to patch yourself up.",
  "675f93f1d40d1e0ee8bc1b25 acceptMT": "I don't think I needed to be asked this...",

  "675f95176d42d89508a92b49 name": "Bled dry",
  "675f95176d42d89508a92b49 description": "You've proved to me that you know how to stop a bleeding. What if you're out of supplies, though? Can you survive that serious loss of blood pressure and energy? Try not to pass out in the process.",
  "675f95839596429cc94eb70d": "Survive a heavy bleed for five minutes",
  "675f95176d42d89508a92b49 successMT": "Why on earth did you listen to me? Goodness, you look pale as a sheet. Please tell me you have a bloodbag somewhere.",
  "675f95176d42d89508a92b49 acceptMT": "What is this supposed to accomplish?",

  "675f95ee44f9feda02d1b557 name": "Never again",
  "675f95ee44f9feda02d1b557 description": "I still can't believe you survived that. Just how on earth does your body regenerate from such wounds? Even losing so much blood, you kept going. I don't understand yet, but I don't need to. And I definitely don't need to see you bleed that much again. I don't think you'd want to either. Prove to me that you know how to fix yourself up, including your bones.",
  "675f960a19d277e8821b85f0": "Use any bleed or fracture-fixing item 25 times (exlcuding medkits)",
  "675f95ee44f9feda02d1b557 successMT": "Not enough.",
  "675f95ee44f9feda02d1b557 acceptMT": "Something a little more agreeable...",

  "675f9624d456e1f9110c5a84 name": "To be free from death",
  "675f9624d456e1f9110c5a84 description": "More, more! Not just blood, not just broken bones, I want everything!! Do you even know what its like watching you die so many times? Do you even know you're dying? How many times can you die so painfully, so slowly, and still go out there guns blazing? What is wrong with you? You have to know how to use EVERYTHING to keep yourself alive!",
  "675f96440b7088b7f252b7a4": "Use an AI-2 30 times",
  "675f9651e52dddc6d32ba7a1": "Use a CAR 30 times",
  "675f966b7f2c782221925815": "Use an IFAK 30 times",
  "675f9676fe096f36ab84b341": "Use an AFAK 30 times",
  "675f968acf842085d3cea2da": "Use a Salewa 30 times",
  "675f9695ab1b955db5ec3051": "Use a Grizzly 30 times",
  "675f96a0025937005bda863f": "Use an Aseptic bandage 5 times",
  "675f96adbbfd0e7d88265977": "Use an Army bandage 5 times",
  "675f96c5e1762e98f03ed0eb": "Use an Esmarch 5 times",
  "675f96d151ab3ec123f5f698": "Use a CAT 5 times",
  "675f96d56af8bc0388549237": "Use a CALOK 5 times",
  "675f96e5d29337d04a331ef8": "Use an Immobilizing splint 5 times",
  "675f96ef897646e20a94c77e": "Use an Aluminum  5 times",
  "675f96fda1cf19e0537d8621": "Use a CMS kit twice",
  "675f97087be4e2a0f9ae0b1f": "Use a SURV-12 kit twice",
  "675f971b42e3cd8f53092cb7": "Use any stimulant that provides health regen 8 times.",
  "675f9624d456e1f9110c5a84 successMT": "Yes! Thank you. Keep yourself alive, for your own sake? I wasn't kidding when I said I don't like seeing you die. If I haven't told you already, I don't particularly care for blood and death and corpses, not least the blood and corpse of someone I'm suppose to be helping. Having to watch you die all the time is painful... so die less, alright?",
  "675f9624d456e1f9110c5a84 acceptMT": "I didn't know I could piss off an angel...",

  //Practical Quest Locales

  "675f9c24b899eb8bfaa57771 name": "Taking a night off",
  "675f9c24b899eb8bfaa57771 description": "The art of moving silently is a lot less artistic when you're carrying the weight of dead men's souls on your back. Oh, also their guns and gear. Regardless, knowing how to move quietly will save your life more often than you think. Especially if those you are fighting are more... SAIN than usual, if you know what I mean. Learn how to kill your enemey without them knowing where it came from. Let's start easily, with the assistance of the night.",
  "675f9c43bee183a11d37c705": "Kill 10 enemies between 9PM-4AM",
  "675f9c24b899eb8bfaa57771 successMT": "Getting familiar with the evening times? Good, there's a lot more of it in your near future. Don't forget to sleep at some point.",
  "675f9c24b899eb8bfaa57771 acceptMT": "Not like I had a sleep schedule to begin with",

  "675f9d45ca2e32afe77e1d67 name": "Silent night",
  "675f9d45ca2e32afe77e1d67 description": "The darkness is nice and all, but you know what I just thought of? The darkness doesn't conceal how loud your gun is. Or how loud you are. I mean, the whole point of *covert* movement is to be quiet, sneaky? Show me how it's done.",
  "675f9d6d44eb075413215fad": "Kill 15 enemies between 9PM-4AM while using a suppressor",
  "6830e46d053a17b80fc14cdc": "Kill 15 enemies while in covert movement",
  "675f9d45ca2e32afe77e1d67 successMT": "Wow, that was so quiet I was able to sleep through the night. Thanks",
  "675f9d45ca2e32afe77e1d67 acceptMT": "What if I was already using a suppressor?",

  "675f9d80ef73fbac97959390 name": "So many ways to move (and kill)",
  "675f9d80ef73fbac97959390 description": "There's a lot of different ways you can manipulate your body to provide momentum. There's quite a lot of speeds you can do it at, as well. Not only are most of these ways helpful for movement, but sometimes it's advantages for killing, getting a good angle on your opponent. Let's see just how well you can take advantage of the terrain around you.",
  "675f9e1348d3a6f7f70a4097": "Move 400 units in covert movement",
  "6830e6198e0576ed56c363a2": "Kill 40 enemies while in covert movement",
  "6830e61bfd3a04a684e75350": "Move 300 units while crouched",
  "6830e61c3b49e55256583b1a": "Kill 30 enemies while crouched",
  "6830e61c7ea434fd66b2437b": "Move 50 units while prone",
  "6830e61d1c49f3ceb90a5b04": "Kill 10 enemies while prone",
  "6830e61d012f120d2ba35e9c": "Kill an enemy while blind firing",
  "675f9d80ef73fbac97959390 successMT": "Hehe, look at you squirming all over the place. That's how you do it, though. Put aside how it looks, it helps you survive.",
  "675f9d80ef73fbac97959390 acceptMT": "Oh, lovely.",

  "675f9e3d5139b3c4edbdfd5a name": "Spectre",
  "675f9e3d5139b3c4edbdfd5a description": "Alright, we've gotten plenty of practice, and I've shown you everything there is to be learned about stealth. Now, I have a fun challenge for you. Go to the customs or the mall, and kill three of those PMC guys. The catch? You can't get hurt whatsoever. If you get shot once, you gotta retry. If you break your leg, that's not quiet enough, and you're an idiot. I'd say 'Godspeed' to you, but that won't help this time.",
  "675f9e5d0b0169a7d2784858": "Kill 3 PMCs in one night raid, on Customs or Interchange, with a suppressor, without taking damage",
  "675f9e3d5139b3c4edbdfd5a successMT": "Perfection. You are a terror in the night.",
  "675f9e3d5139b3c4edbdfd5a acceptMT": "Anyone remember the Spectre from BO1? Just me? Alright...",

  "675f9e7ac72aad589029aceb name": "A shadow in the daylight",
  "675f9e7ac72aad589029aceb description": "The night is now yours, you strike all and are seen by none. A myth, an urban legend. The spectre of Tarkov. Unfortunately for you, the night doesn't last forever. Sometimes, it isn't even an option. Can the spectre haunt during the day, or will the sun protect the inhabitants of Tarkov?",
  "675f9f31d6dd3b948bc558b9": "Kill 6 enemies in one raid on Customs, Reserve, or Interchange, with a suppressor, without taking damage",
  "675f9e7ac72aad589029aceb successMT": "And thus, a new Tarkov legend is born. Go on, Shadow of Tarkov.",
  "675f9e7ac72aad589029aceb acceptMT": "Finally. Vitaman D",

  "675fa57b9341fd1dca361a9a name": "Basic Medication",
  "675fa57b9341fd1dca361a9a description": "Considering you have a hideout, you sure learn how to make good use of it. You've built some modules by now, correct? Let me show you how to use it efficiently. We'll start off with some essentials, like medical supplies. Go make a few things at that medstation of yours, stuff you might bring into raid.",
  "675fa595691ad4b512bdbec9": "Complete 2 crafts at the Medstation",
  "675fa57b9341fd1dca361a9a successMT": "There you go! See if those help you out later today.",
  "675fa57b9341fd1dca361a9a acceptMT": "Y'know, I don't know if I like you watching me in my hideout...",

  "675fa5d912e50296e7a6a7fe name": "A Proper Utilization of Resources",
  "675fa5d912e50296e7a6a7fe description": "You know how to craft some basic medication, and that's good! But there's a lot more you can do in this place. You can make ammo, armor, even entire weapons! Not to mention other important things like food, water, and things you can sell for profit. Let's try using all your workstations, really get you familiar with what you're working with.",
  "675fa5eb2046a3caa43abf56": "Complete 30 total non-cyclic crafts",
  "675fa5f1c24382df8bb7bbef": "Complete 3 crafts at the Workbench",
  "68e4b530b0d9185ff5a3dd8b": "Complete 3 crafts at the Lavatory",
  "68e4b53245152bf16f608f3f": "Complete 3 crafts at the Medstation",
  "68e4b5339d9c7ad90beefd03": "Complete 3 crafts at the Kitchen",
  "68e4b532d625edb06e5e428c": "Complete 1 craft at the Intelligence Center",
  "675fa5d912e50296e7a6a7fe successMT": "How about that? You got a whole factory going on in there, you can make just about anything you want. ...Hmm, y'know, 'factory' gives me an idea.",
  "675fa5d912e50296e7a6a7fe acceptMT": "You know what they say about idle hands...",

  "675fa60bb1e9c2a40d8049f3 name": "This Totally Isn't a Factorio Reference",
  "675fa60bb1e9c2a40d8049f3 description": "Why do all this work yourself when you can have machines do it for you over time? I mean, let's ignore the fact that crafting seems to already happen automatically here; don't worry about that. Let's try *actual* automation, letting the station truly do it for you. There's three available in your hideout; put each of them to work.",
  "675fa84e5034cc5e4042b8bd": "Collect Bitcoin three times",
  "675fa8547a5e687ffadf337b": "Collect Purified Water ten times",
  "68e4c748486304c76fa05e07": "Collect Moonshine ten times (don't drink it all at once...)",
  "675fa60bb1e9c2a40d8049f3 successMT": "If only you could craft an ammo case, haha! You're not going to have any ammo shortages for a while now, that's for sure. I just hope the quality is good enough, I know some of that ammunition can be... slightly less effective against some of the beefier dudes out there. Also, don't forget that the PMM can only be fired out of the klin, not the kedr",
  "675fa60bb1e9c2a40d8049f3 acceptMT": "New quest: Come back in five days. Sure, thanks Guiding Light.",

  "675fa988547274883ee636e7 name": "We Needed a 4th Crafting Quest",
  "675fa988547274883ee636e7 description": "Oh, there's a fourth one of these? I ran out of ideas for this branch. Shoot, uhm... ... ... Oh, screw it. Just go make a bunch of stuff, I don't really care. You know how hard it is to come up with unique ideas every time? If I could make you craft specific things, that'd be nice, but that's hell itself to do. Go make 100 AI-2s for all I care.",
  "675fa9a199cf33415fd10066": "Complete 100 non-cyclic crafts",
  "68e4d1394f78b5fd27ca9e51": "Complete 30 cyclic crafts",
  "675fa988547274883ee636e7 successMT": "... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ... ..Oh, you did it. Uhm, well done! You're a, uh, a master crafter now. Yeah.",
  "675fa988547274883ee636e7 acceptMT": "Work kills creativity, I suppose.",

  "675fabf283c1878c0fc117cd name": "Protection is Paramount",
  "675fabf283c1878c0fc117cd description": "I'll be honest, I don't personally care for the heavy vests as much. They're just so, well... heavy. However, I cannot deny the sheer armour they provide, and that can be just as useful as mobility. Let's get you outfitted, shall we?",
  "675fac1dbc53db9b8a8b2a76": "Kill 10 enemies while wearing heavy armour vests / rigs",
  "675fabf283c1878c0fc117cd successMT": "Glad to see you're comfortable in these things. Onto the next one.",
  "675fabf283c1878c0fc117cd acceptMT": "Heavy to wear, but heavy to knock down.",

  "675face55d964e1a7ac431ee name": "3D defense",
  "675face55d964e1a7ac431ee description": "If you're going through the trouble of wearing a heavy vest, you should probably wear one that actually protects every side of you. It seems pretty silly to have all that hard work bypassed by some scav who caught you from a bad angle. Some of the armour here can support side plates, see how you like them.",
  "675fad063bf89efffc855ce5": "Kill 20 enemies while wearing a vest that can hold all 4 plates in (front, back, l side, r side)",
  "675face55d964e1a7ac431ee successMT": "Well, what were the results? Did you find yourself dying less often?",
  "675face55d964e1a7ac431ee acceptMT": "Sure hope my spine holds up",

  "675fad1851a1c2dbbe69e28e name": "Anti-material",
  "675fad1851a1c2dbbe69e28e description": "Knowing how to wear heavy armour vests is nice and all, but knowing how to take it down is good too. Armour is great for you, but not so great when an enemy is wearing it. I want you to not only wear down their armour, but show me you know how to get around it as well.",
  "675fad38c0c80b59b871da6c": "Deal a total of 1000 damage to enemy armour.",
  "6830ea0d0bfe7329ebdc82c5": "Kill 20 enemies with leg or arm shots.",
  "675fad1851a1c2dbbe69e28e successMT": "Look at all that metal and ceramic on the floor. Think I saw a guy's arm on the counter as well. Very well done.",
  "675fad1851a1c2dbbe69e28e acceptMT": "Now we get to have a bit of fun.",

  "675fadf1778e4ca1f16b9938 name": "Plate up!",
  "675fadf1778e4ca1f16b9938 description": "Y'know... armour is really only as good as the plate you put into it. Those big vests you wore for me last time... what did you have in them? Were you able to find nice, tier 6 plates? Or did you have to settle for some tier 4? Well, either way, let's get you some tier 6 ones. There's quite a few, each with different properties. Can you find one of each? I don't expect them brand new, don't worry. Take 'em off someone you kill, or not. Heck, if you wanna cheat, get em from a vendor or the market. The goal is to supply you with good protection, so, whatever accomplishes that.",
  "675fae32ce2dfd0d7e6668ea": "Hand over an ESAPI level IV ballistic plate",
  "675fae3aea1047ed0e632569": "Hand over a Kiba Arms Steel ballistic plate",
  "675fae3f23307f8296421b8b": "Hand over a NESCO 4400-SA-MC ballistic plate",
  "675fae4d4ea4199d69436dc6": "Hand over a KITECO SC-IV SA ballistic plate",
  "675fae53c27fa88735787444": "Hand over a GAC 4sss2 ballistic plate",
  "675fae58b20d945fac2111e6": "Hand over a Granit Br5 ballistic plate",
  "675fae5de9a1b0a2088be33d": "Hand over a Cult Termite ballistic plate",
  "675fadf1778e4ca1f16b9938 successMT": "Notice how there's some differences between the top tiers? Different weights, durabilities... pick what you like.",
  "675fadf1778e4ca1f16b9938 acceptMT": "hv4 accept, I can't think of one rn",

  "675faf25d43c38f8ec713af8 name": "A True Juggernaut",
  "675faf25d43c38f8ec713af8 description": "Alright. We've got the plates, we've got the practice, now we execute it. I have a special challenge for you, so listen closely. First, you need a vest that has every armour zone possible. Shoulders, Neck, Groin, the whole nine yards. Then, all four sides need tier 6 plates. Doesn't matter which ones, just gotta be class 6. *Then*, you need either the Altyn or Rys-T helmet WITH the face shield installed. Once you've got all that, head to any map you like, and knock out 15 people. You gotta get at least 1 pmc in the mix, otherwise it's just boring.",
  "675fafdbc326769212410094": "Kill 15 enemies in ONE raid using the described gear (READ THE DESCRIPTION!)",
  "6a69e71b243e4d1a999be424": "Ensure one of them is a PMC.",
  "675faf25d43c38f8ec713af8 successMT": "Hah! They couldn't do anything against you, you might as well have been invincible.'",
  "675faf25d43c38f8ec713af8 acceptMT": "They should've had their own fancy armour",

  "675fb07fcdea44ae4beb0310 name": "Finding materials",
  "675fb07fcdea44ae4beb0310 description": "Gotten some work done on your hideout, I see! But, I know you have more to go. Find some additional parts for the rest of your hideout.",
  "675fb0e9c104b7e7773b4fd0": "'Hand over' 5 bolts",
  "675fb1089c79a949b0210a65": "'Hand over' 5 nuts",
  "675fb10f5b14a1aeea564fb1": "'Hand over' 5 metal parts",
  "675fb11d1a9e100a65ccd610": "'Hand over' 2 corrugated hoses",
  "675fb07fcdea44ae4beb0310 successMT": "You should be able to build a few things with those! It'll be a good start, don't you think?",
  "675fb07fcdea44ae4beb0310 acceptMT": "I've been reduced to an errand boy.",

  "675fb1692d56a22cb5050420 name": "Keeping the lights on",
  "675fb1692d56a22cb5050420 description": "You're starting to have a real operation going on here! You're making things, producing rations, really starting to thrive in the beautiful landscape of Tarkov. I want to make sure that you have enough resources to keep your little facility running. Looks like you needs filters and fuel.",
  "675fb182a957b882e68f9c77": "'Hand over' two FIR air filters",
  "675fb18618c10723081a4ed8": "'Hand over' 10 FIR water filters",
  "675fb18d6959d6a7c07b222e": "'Hand over' 5 FIR fuel cans (either one)",
  "675fb1692d56a22cb5050420 successMT": "Wonderful! Glad to see you've got plenty of backstock for your hideout",
  "675fb1692d56a22cb5050420 acceptMT": "Where exactly does this stuff 'go' when I hand it it?",

  "675fb1f7b13493767439b1e9 name": "Raking it in",
  "675fb1f7b13493767439b1e9 description": "You must have quite a nice place by now! Are ya winnin, son? Anyways, I heard there's a way to, erm, 'mine bitcoin'. I don't have any record of 'bitcoin' being a resource harvestable from the earth's crust, but apparently computers can do it? I don't understand what you humans come up with some times... Well, regardless, being able to mine it means your hideout is very far along. Let me know when you reach this stage.",
  "675fb20275e4da479deaea95": "Collect bitcoin from the hideout once",
  "675fb1f7b13493767439b1e9 successMT": "It's a 'digital currency', you say? I don't even know, I shouldn't have asked... you can get away with anything nowadays. Hah, maybe you'll start selling pictures next. ...What's that look for?",
  "675fb1f7b13493767439b1e9 acceptMT": "This might take a while",

  "675fb2b1f6959c00773c9351 name": "Mobility is Marvelous",
  "675fb2b1f6959c00773c9351 description": "Light vests are likely what I would wear, if I was stuck in your situation. I personally care more about mobility than sheer defense. I don't need to be able to tank shots if I'm not getting shot, right? Being able to maneruver quickly is so important, especially since you're stuck here by yourself. Let's get you comfortable with these lighter vests and rigs, eh?",
  "675fb2da336204b63c82e778": "Kill 10 enemies while wearing a light armour vest / rig",
  "675fb2b1f6959c00773c9351 successMT": "Yeah, you're getting the hang of it! Let's get a little more specialized",
  "675fb2b1f6959c00773c9351 acceptMT": "Alliteration is Amazing",

  "675fb306731c2f7abc914ab7 name": "Light as a feather",
  "675fb306731c2f7abc914ab7 description": "Isn't it funnt that some 'light armour' really isn't that light? I mean, sure, some plates are made of armor steel, I don't expect that to be as light as a feather. But some small, weak plates still end up weighing more than they are worth. Beyond that, some vests end up weighing a lot just from all the 'soft' armour they have. Why don't you go try wearing light stuff? You might enjoy the newfound speed.",
  "675fb3228734d45cbff0096c": "Kill 20 enemies while wearing only plates that weight <2KG, in a vest that *BY ITSELF* weighs <5KG.",
  "675fb306731c2f7abc914ab7 successMT": "Well, how about it? Can be nice when you're trying to offset big guns, ammo, and have more left over for all that loot you'll pick up in raid. It matters less as you work on your strength, though.",
  "675fb306731c2f7abc914ab7 acceptMT": "Stealth is a vital part of Metal Gear Solid Online for all players",

  "675fb3380bc5ea0c58037ae4 name": "Pellets B gone",
  "675fb3380bc5ea0c58037ae4 description": "Class 2 armour is... pretty bad, I won't lie. However, it's usually the lightest armour you can get, while still protecting you from weak rounds that most scavs will be firing at you, as well as some early level PMCs. Knowing how to effectively use these weaker armour can really help out, especially for the rougher seasons when you're on a budget.",
  "675fb35328d4ebba9b33df73": "Kill 25 enemies while wearing the 6B2, Module-3M, or PACA armour.",
  "675fb3380bc5ea0c58037ae4 successMT": "What'd you think? Super light, but keeps the shotguns and pistols away",
  "675fb3380bc5ea0c58037ae4 acceptMT": "Buy now, and you'll get a second class 2 armour for free!",

  "675fb39d87632dbd67518472 name": "Preparing repairs",
  "675fb39d87632dbd67518472 description": "As much as these armour vests are all about not getting shot in the first place, it's still bound to happen eventually. You should have a repair kit on standby for when you get ambushed by a group of scavs with shotguns. Find two, while you're at it. Having a backup is important!",
  "675fb3b3c0d4445da77de019": "Find 2 armour repair kits FIR",
  "675fb39d87632dbd67518472 successMT": "Sweet! Just those should last you a long time. Don't forget to find another one BEFORE you run out of repairing, though.",
  "675fb39d87632dbd67518472 acceptMT": "I suppose those would be important.",

  "675fb3c2af09ce7f0cde82f7 name": "The truly stylish one",
  "675fb3c2af09ce7f0cde82f7 description": "I have a fun idea. You know Killa, right? Everyone loves Killa. Anyways, they call him 'The Stylish One', like he's some kind of idol. Supposedly it's because of his unique outfit? But he hides it behind all that armour, like he's scared of something... ...I think you know where this is going :D.",
  "675fb5bdf78798ae8cb7a7c8": "Kill Killa while wearing no armour of any kind and survive the raid.",
  "675fb3c2af09ce7f0cde82f7 successMT": "How about that? I think you have become the stylish one. So many vests, and you made them all look good.",
  "675fb3c2af09ce7f0cde82f7 acceptMT": "Killa got nothing on me",

  "675fc396809096d17f73d523 name": "Starting small",
  "675fc396809096d17f73d523 description": "Say what you will about Tarkov, this is real life we're talking about. Your magazines don't magically combine like the video games you grew up on. Here, you gotta take care of them. That means you gotta get good at loading, unloading, and switching mags fast. We'll start off with the lil 10 rounders. Let's do one kill for each bullet you can hold.",
  "675fc3ad6bb21a35d5ff5e79": "Kill 10 enemies while using 10 round mags",
  "675fc396809096d17f73d523 successMT": "Less is more, they say. If you have a 10 round magazine, it's lighter, likely more ergonomic, and most importantly will cause you to think more carefully about your shots. In that way, a 10 round magazine can be way more effective than a larger one.",
  "675fc396809096d17f73d523 acceptMT": "Sure hope 10 is enough",

  "675fc3d75a1902a5198972d2 name": "Upgrades, people",
  "675fc3d75a1902a5198972d2 description": "The 10 rounders were nice, but sometimes that's just not enough ammo to seal the deal. Let's double the amount of bullets we can use, how about that? Still low enough that you'll be a little more careful, but plenty incase you miss a few or if the enemy is heavily armoured.",
  "675fc3e85deec3e207705dbc": "Kill 20 enemies while using 20 round mags",
  "675fc3d75a1902a5198972d2 successMT": "So, do you prefer the 10 or the 20 so far? Perhaps the 20 allows different guns that didn't have access to 10 rounds.",
  "675fc3d75a1902a5198972d2 acceptMT": "Upgrades.",

  "675fc4671d4d9f752600b233 name": "Standard Issue",
  "675fc4671d4d9f752600b233 description": "Alright, now let's get used to what you're most commonly be working with. Normally I'd stick with the whole 'one kill per capacity' thing, but 30 round magazines are standard issue, so I think it's the most important capacity to be familiar with. How about you double what you'd normally do?",
  "675fc478f7756d3e8d55cba5": "Kill 60 enemies while using 30 round mags",
  "675fc4671d4d9f752600b233 successMT": "Was the extra work so bad? I told you, 30 round mags are everywhere. So many guns can use them.",
  "675fc4671d4d9f752600b233 acceptMT": "More killing, less complaining",

  "675fc4911d57f88ea5ad6b57 name": "50 dead men",
  "675fc4911d57f88ea5ad6b57 description": "How about something more fun? 50 rounders aren't as common, but you can still find plenty of weapons that use them. More bullets means you lose out on the 'bonuses' the smaller mags give you, but more bullets! Who's going to complain about more bullets?",
  "675fc4aff65bea3c9622108a": "Kill 50 enemies while using 50 round mags",
  "675fc4911d57f88ea5ad6b57 successMT": "You have killed 120 people for this training so far. You'd think this is a combat taskline, at this rate.",
  "675fc4911d57f88ea5ad6b57 acceptMT": "P90 gang",

  "675fc4cbc0b5b5986ad901a6 name": "Overkill",
  "675fc4cbc0b5b5986ad901a6 description": "Hot take: If you need 60 round magazines, you either found yourself in a REALLY bad situation, or you need to work on your aim. Oh well, they exist, and sometimes you just really need to suppress a location. Don't waste all your ammo, though! That stuff can be expensive.",
  "675fc4e36682376cbfb02211": "Kill 60 enemies while using 60 round mags",
  "675fc4cbc0b5b5986ad901a6 successMT": "Mag drills complete! You should have no issue transferring these skills to the more unusual magazine capacities, I believe in you.",
  "675fc4cbc0b5b5986ad901a6 acceptMT": "To be fair, 60 is quite a lot",

  "68015ed9ab0091eae8610a5c name": "Mystery Box",
  "68015ed9ab0091eae8610a5c description": "Searching seems like a valuable skill to have here. You're still searching for an answer to some things right now, aren't you? Sorry, sorry. Well... Hmm. Let's start with the basics. Go open some containers and see what's inside. Make sure you move everything around a bunch and make a ton of noise like a trained military soldier would (BSG why is looting so loud~)",
  "68015f02a39f8fe1b474339f": "Search 20 containers",
  "68015ef89165025cc710477f": "Pickup 40 items",
  "68015ed9ab0091eae8610a5c successMT": "Good, glad to see you know how to open a lid. Or a backpack. Or a drawer. Or a - whatever, you know what you're doing.",
  "68015ed9ab0091eae8610a5c acceptMT": "If only I could find a Ray Gun in one of these boxes...",

  "6801632874f58ba54e659d68 name": "Thorough Investigation",
  "6801632874f58ba54e659d68 description": "If tasked with searching one specific area in painstaking detail, how would you fare? Could you find the needle in the haystack? Or will the lack of dopamine burn you out? Let's see.",
  "680163c6cd109f2aec2aadee": "Search 60 containers in one raid",
  "6801632874f58ba54e659d68 successMT": "So you can dedicate your time to such a task, if needed. You will find this to be a valuable skill indeed.",
  "6801632874f58ba54e659d68 acceptMT": "ugh.",

  "680175d47d02823b26130bb4 name": "Casting a wide net",
  "680175d47d02823b26130bb4 description": "You can search a small area with great precision, and that's good. What's also good is being able to search a much larger area to an only slightly lesser level of detail. Let's see what we can find within Tarkov.",
  "6801760d12c9b46e895ff05d": "Search 300 containers total",
  "680178d4d889b0191ef9892a": "Loot 1000 items total",
  "680178c761c3be112eadcd99": "Search 25 containers on Customs and / or Steets",
  "680178b8011e6765f3666d43": "Search 25 containers on Interchange and / or Lighthouse",
  "680178ae0eeb23174f940bf6": "Search 15 containers on Reserve",
  "6801789e3a92bec468c2e424": "Loot 40 items from Woods and / or Shoreline",
  "6801785c65dcf5ce598b031b": "Loot 40 items from Ground Zero and / or Factory",
  "680177df14ddfedb5fe2b68c": "Loot 30 items from The Lab",
  "680175d47d02823b26130bb4 successMT": "Well done. You should have a rough idea of what Tarkov looks like now, if you didn't already.",
  "680175d47d02823b26130bb4 acceptMT": "Aren't there enough quests about running around the whole place? Yeesh.",

  "GL_PR_SE4 name": "A Game of Hide and Seek",
  "GL_PR_SE4 description": "The final search quest... ...hmm. Alright, let's go non-canon for a bit. Consider the 4th wall broken, player, cause I'm gonna tell you exactly how this works. I have hidden a wooden cross somewhere in Tarkov. Dynamic Maps can't find it, and the location moves on each update, unless no one has found it yet. I'll provide you the map it's on and a single hint. Good luck. (CURRENT MAP: Customs. CURRENT HINT: 'In a building where many have been deceived')",
  "GL_PR_SE4 task1": "Find the cross and turn it in.",
  "GL_PR_SE4 successMT": "Oho! Well done. Very, very well done.",
  "GL_PR_SE4 acceptMT": "Well that's just fantatsic.",

  "6760617dcc9bc82484dbfef9 name": "Preparing for the worst",
  "6760617dcc9bc82484dbfef9 description": "Tarkov, being real life, is a rather unique place. It turns out that getting shot has consequences. Who'dve thought, right? If you're going to get shot, it's going to mess you up, and you need to know how to get yourself back in working order. First, we need the right tools. Go get some surgical kits, a few of each.",
  "676061969309d1cfe0953d74": "Acquire 5 CMS kits",
  "6760619c51ccf0944b47730c": "Acquire 3 SURV-12 kits",
  "6760617dcc9bc82484dbfef9 successMT": "Some of the red, some of the black... We'll be using most of these, don't worry. That's not what you're worried about? Ah, you can't die, you'll be fine",
  "6760617dcc9bc82484dbfef9 acceptMT": "Wait, how are we going to train this...?",

  "676061d0276d9949c9db2409 name": "Field practice",
  "676061d0276d9949c9db2409 description": "Now that you have the tools, let's get to work. I'm afraid there's only going to be one person you can practice on... erm... do what you must.",
  "676061f2813bd1dc69426a6c": "Use a CMS kit 5 times",
  "676061f7360beec9d45be8bc": "Use a SURV-12 kit 5 times",
  "676061d0276d9949c9db2409 successMT": "Yeah, you're getting the hang of it! Let's keep working, there's plenty more to practice.",
  "676061d0276d9949c9db2409 acceptMT": "I suppose it's useful, but I wish we could do this in a way that didn't involve me getting shot a lot?",

  "6760620f57313ab593494020 name": "Preemptive measures",
  "6760620f57313ab593494020 description": "Being proficient at surgery is awesome, but do you know what's even more awesome? Not needing to do surgery at all. Yeah, crazy thought. A great way to avoid doing surgery is to take care of your wounds before your whole arm falls off. How about that, just healing normally?",
  "67606224f12ae4625dd45576": "Regain 3000 health",
  "6760620f57313ab593494020 successMT": "Good! Knowing how to do surgery is good, but not needing to do surgery is even better. Try to keep it that way, eh?",
  "6760620f57313ab593494020 acceptMT": "Why are we writing quests where I have to take damage? What sadist is causing this?",

  "6760623cf0d6c8929a33586f name": "A different kind of 'surgical'",
  "6760623cf0d6c8929a33586f description": "You know, so far these tasks have been sort of... out of your control, I guess? Like, you could just be jumping off buildings to do this, but I don't imagine you're doing that very often, that's no fun. So, how about a different kind of surgical? It's technically cheating, but hey, I really can only think of so many ways to make training surgery interesting. We'll get back to the grind next task, but let's have some fun for a bit, ok? I want 8 headshots, with bolt-actions, in the same raid. That's quite surgical, eh?",
  "6760625aa0c6b14cad492140": "Kill 8 enemies with headshots with bolt-action rifles in a single raid.",
  "6760623cf0d6c8929a33586f successMT": "Good shooting, m8. Back to the less fun stuff, sadly.",
  "6760623cf0d6c8929a33586f acceptMT": "That is... technically a slang definition of surgical, I guess. Oh well, beats jumping off the roof 50 times.",

  "6760627b1549e58187af6c8b name": "Back to the grind",
  "6760627b1549e58187af6c8b description": "I hope last task was a little more enjoyable, a nice break from what we're doing. Unfortunately, there's really only one way I can actually train you on your surgery... and that's to do surgery. So, being the final task, I really have no choice but to do it that way. I highly recommend letting this one happen naturally, it will over time. You're not missing out by not completing your training, if you think about it. If you don't need to be performing surgery, you don't need to be an expert in surgery. It's up to you if you even want to go for it, honestly.",
  "67606297a3ee72a2bb69d26b": "Perform surgery a total of 60 times",
  "6760629c6eb07e736107efe5": "At least 10 with the CMS",
  "676062ae9acfef31ba814419": "At least 15 with the SURV-12",
  "6760627b1549e58187af6c8b successMT": "Well, that's done now. You can probably be a surgeon now, once you get out of here. Also, you moved you liver into the wrong place when repairing your stomach that one time. I wonder if that'll fix itself or not when you die again? We'll fine out.",
  "6760627b1549e58187af6c8b acceptMT": "That's a lot of roofs to jump off of, I guess. (This is not actually the intended way to complete this, please don't do that)",

  "675fbf81418ccd759e3acb88 name": "Kitting out",
  "675fbf81418ccd759e3acb88 description": "Taking care of your weapons is by far one of the best things you can do to improve your chances of survival in Tarkov. They're what's keeping you alive, so you should keep them alive, too! To do this, though, you'll need the right tools. I'm sure there's some sort of repair kit out there, right? Normally I wouldn't fuss about whether it's brand new or 'found in raid' or whatever, but this is important enough that you should find, or craft, it yourself.",
  "675fbfa07ce0132ea7d75329": "'Hand over' a FIR Weapon Repair Kit",
  "675fbf81418ccd759e3acb88 successMT": "Yeah, that looks right! Before we use it, though, I think I should show you why it's so important.",
  "675fbf81418ccd759e3acb88 acceptMT": "It has a point, I really should be taking care of them.",

  "675fbfbdea962c75b32871e8 name": "Ol' (un)reliable",
  "675fbfbdea962c75b32871e8 description": "Have you ever used a weapon for so long that it barely works anymore? It jams, it breaks down, it misfires, it just shouldn't be relied upon for combat. Sometimes, studying such a weapon can be of great value for understanding future weapon repairs, as well as being a grim reminder of what can happen if you don't take proper care of your firearm. Try wearing a weapon down to scrap. You might want to bring another weapon in while you do this...",
  "675fbfbdea962c75b32871e8": "Hand in an AR or SMG with <2 durability remaining",
  "675fbfbdea962c75b32871e8 successMT": "Wow, look at that thing. Do you even want it back? Well, I can't exactly take it... just go leave it by your workbench, I guess.",
  "675fbfbdea962c75b32871e8 acceptMT": "This is going to be interesting",

  "675fc1b38aba4c1eef51eeda name": "Reduced to the base parts",
  "675fc1b38aba4c1eef51eeda description": "Have you ever seen a disassembled weapon before? I sure hope you have, given that you are a trained military guy and all that. Being able to identify various weapon parts is critical to being able to effectively repair your weapon. Try taking some weapons apart, or even better, try finding some new ones in raid. Buy a VPO-209 from Skier and deconstruct it at your workbench, see what you get.",
  "675fc1c704637875ee6e269f": "'Hand over' 15 FIR weapon parts",
  "675fc1b38aba4c1eef51eeda successMT": "Look at all that metal! I think you've seen enough scrap and oil to know exactly what to look out for when repairing your weapon, so let's go do it.",
  "675fc1b38aba4c1eef51eeda acceptMT": "I should deconstruct some weapons at the workbench for this.",

  "675fc21e55efcbded71ed6a6 name": "Omnicaliber",
  "675fc21e55efcbded71ed6a6 description": "You know what we haven't really done yet? Practied with all of the different weapons. 'But light, why don't we use weapon repair kits?' Because it doesn't work. So instead, you're gonna learn about the different calibers of weapons. I want you to grab some kills with every caliber you can find. I'll spare you the grenade launchers, at least.",
  "675fc22e23900a949def81e9": "Kill 5 enemies with 20/70 (TOZ is the only one)",
  "675fc2386297be1e4eaa6af0": "Kill 5 enemies with 12/70",
  "675fc2451f539018f5553415": "Kill 5 enemies with 23x75mm (KS-23 is the only one)",
  "675fc249944d61dfbe37a8f7": "Kill 5 enemies with 7.62x25mm Tokarev",
  "675fc2588619854557c0d59f": "Kill 5 enemies with 9x18mm Makarov",
  "675fc25d94c006d222b4fa65": "Kill 5 enemies with 9x19mm Parabellum",
  "675fc26affb0838b3b14e7c9": "Kill 5 enemies with 9x21mm Gyurza",
  "675fc2703339e9f772803c50": "Kill 5 enemies with .357 Magnum",
  "675fc284a3da32303660c860": "Kill 5 enemies with .45 ACP",
  "675fc28951eb4e5fafc39995": "Kill 5 enemies with 4.6x30mm HK",
  "675fc2a4cfbb5585a8d6b9b7": "Kill 5 enemies with 5.7x28mm FN",
  "675fc2aeb04b26df091a66fe": "Kill 5 enemies with 5.45x39mm",
  "675fc2baf64aa80c68b6e00b": "Kill 5 enemies with 5.56x45mm NATO",
  "675fc2c061ffe868f0e8682d": "Kill 5 enemies with 6.8x51mm (MCX SPEAR is the only one)",
  "675fc2d15f364c8396a30128": "Kill 5 enemies with .300 Blackout",
  "675fc2d7033a1c6c40764741": "Kill 5 enemies with 7.62x39mm",
  "675fc2e6f63ca8b1d58cc91e": "Kill 5 enemies with 7.62x51mm NATO",
  "675fc2ea1a51e8bf07563b13": "Kill 5 enemies with 7.62x54mmR",
  "675fc2f8f6e5651201cf8ecf": "Kill 5 enemies with .338 Lapua Magnum",
  "675fc2fc8552dac52799713b": "Kill 5 enemies with 9x39mm",
  "675fc30de691ce2caadafff0": "Kill 5 enemies with .366 TKM",
  "675fc312065a8e06a1dea93b": "Kill 5 enemies with 12.7x55mm STs-130",
  "675fc32286fd083448930ae5": "Kill 5 enemies with .50 Action Express",
  "675fc21e55efcbded71ed6a6 successMT": "Got a feel for each one, have ya? Can you tell their strenghts and weaknesses? Ah well, the next one should be enjoyable.",
  "675fc21e55efcbded71ed6a6 acceptMT": "Seems... easy? Is there a catch? Ehhh, some calibers aren't the easiest to get, I suppose.",

  "675fbe872ded86d087f3accf name": "Death.",
  "675fbe872ded86d087f3accf description": "...",
  "675fbeb4df1f0155dcdb8dc5": "Kill.",
  "675fbe872ded86d087f3accf successMT": "...heh.",
  "675fbe872ded86d087f3accf acceptMT": "...uh, GL? You good?",

  //THESE NEED SORTED!

  "682fde19d7e16e8d09d55e30 name": "Intelligence test!",
  "682fde19d7e16e8d09d55e30 description": "Freebee, this one is fake! The other ones won't be so easy... You'll have to look at all pieces of the quests!",
  "68309d7b8c6433e01562409a": "Click 'turn in' and complete to submit your answer!",
